    {
      "question": "I opened /dashboard and it just says \"Owner access required to view this dashboard.\" Why?",
      "answer": "The Operations Console is for the RackTrack platform owner. The app itself will let an Organization Admin open /dashboard, but the server refuses the data with a 403 and the page shows \"Owner access required to view this dashboard.\" On the Logs tab the equivalent message is \"Admin access required to view logs.\" (The old /logs bookmark now redirects to /dashboard, where Logs is a tab.)\n\nThere is nothing you can change from inside the app \u2014 the role check happens on the server, so no setting in your organization will unlock it. Access is limited to the platform owner, though RackTrack staff can optionally add a specific username to a server-side allow-list if there's a genuine operational need. If you need operational figures for your own organization, contact RackTrack support (the platform owner) to pull them for you or to arrange access.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Owner access required to view this dashboard.",
        "Admin access required to view logs.",
        "HTTP 403 on the dashboard",
        "Console page is blank for an org admin"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The client route /dashboard uses AdminRoute (org_admin OR owner), but the server endpoints /api/admin/dashboard and /api/logs* require role === 'owner' (or a username listed in the AUDIT_ADMINS env allow-list) and return 403 otherwise. The client turns that 403 into the friendly message.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/App.jsx",
          "lines": "86-88",
          "snippet": "if (user?.role !== 'org_admin' && user?.role !== 'owner') {\n    return <Navigate to=\"/\" replace />;\n  }"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/app.js",
          "lines": "1853-1857",
          "snippet": "app.get('/api/admin/dashboard', auth.requireAuth, (req, res) => {\n  const adminUsers = String(process.env.AUDIT_ADMINS || '')\n    .split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  const allowed = req.user.role === 'owner' || adminUsers.includes(req.user.username);\n  if (!allowed) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Owner access required' });"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/DashboardPage.jsx",
          "lines": "79",
          "snippet": "if (res.status === 403) { setError('Owner access required to view this dashboard.'); setLoading(false); return; }"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "150",
          "snippet": "if (logsRes.status === 403) { setError('Admin access required to view logs.'); setLoading(false); return; }"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": false,
      "audience": "admin",
