    {
      "question": "What do the \"Live\" and \"Paused\" buttons do, and how often does the console update itself?",
      "answer": "The button in the top-right toggles auto-refresh. When it reads \"Live\", the console reloads on its own; when you click it, it reads \"Paused\" and stops reloading until you press \"Refresh\" or switch it back to Live.\n\nWhile Live is on, the Operations tab reloads every 5 seconds and the Logs tab every 4 seconds. Separately, the \"x ago\" timestamps tick over once a second, so ages stay accurate even between reloads. \"Refresh\" forces an immediate reload of whichever tab you are on, whether or not Live is on.\n\nPause it when you are reading a specific row and don't want it to move under you.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Rows keep moving while I read them",
        "What does Paused mean",
        "How often does the console refresh",
        "Console updates by itself"
      ],
      "rootCause": "DashboardPage owns `live` and `refreshTick` and passes them to both views; OperationsView polls /api/admin/dashboard on a 5000ms interval and LogsView polls /api/logs on a 4000ms interval, each gated on the live flag, with an independent 1s tick for relative time rendering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/DashboardPage.jsx",
          "lines": "96-106",
          "snippet": "// Poll every 5s while \"live\" is on.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const id = setInterval(() => { if (liveRef.current) load(); }, 5000);\n    return () => clearInterval(id);\n  }, [load]);\n\n  // Independent 1s tick keeps relative timestamps current between polls.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const id = setInterval(() => setTick(t => t + 1), 1000);"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "169-173",
          "snippet": "// Poll every 4s while live.\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const id = setInterval(() => { if (liveRef.current) load(); }, 4000);\n    return () => clearInterval(id);\n  }, [load]);"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/DashboardPage.jsx",
          "lines": "341-348",
          "snippet": "onClick={() => setLive(v => !v)}\n            title={live ? 'Auto-refresh on' : 'Auto-refresh paused'}\n          >\n            <span className={styles.liveDot} />\n            {live ? 'Live' : 'Paused'}"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": true,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
      "_votes": 3,
      "_refuted": 0,
      "id": "OPS-004"
    },
    {
      "question": "In the Live activity feed some rows say \"not signed in\" or show no username. Is that a bug?",
      "answer": "No. The feed records things that happen before anyone is signed in \u2014 sign-in attempts, sign-ups, password resets. Those events have no logged-in session, so RackTrack shows the identifier the person typed (the email or username they entered) and tags the row \"not signed in\". If no identifier was captured with the event, the name column simply reads \"guest\" \u2014 it is never left blank.\n\nOther things you will see in a feed row: a green \"ok\" or red \"fail\" pill, the plain-English action (for example \"Scanned a rack\", \"Located a port\", \"Signed in\", \"Approved an org\", \"Gave feedback\", \"Ran console command\"), the organization, and how long ago it happened. Failed rows also show the error text underneath.\n\nIf an action shows as a dotted machine name (like `logs.clear`) rather than a phrase, that simply means no friendly label has been written for it yet \u2014 the event itself is recorded correctly.",
      "symptoms": [
        "not signed in in the activity feed",
        "Blank username in Live activity",
        "Action shows as a dotted name like scan.create",
        "guest rows in the feed"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The /api/admin/dashboard `recent` query falls back to json_extract(payload,'$.ident') when audit_log.username is empty and sets a guest flag; the client labels those 'not signed in'. Action text is mapped through ACTION_LABELS with a raw-key fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/app.js",
          "lines": "1893-1904",
          "snippet": "// Events at the auth gate (sign-in / sign-up / reset) have no logged-in\n    // session, so username is NULL. We fall back to the *attempted* identifier\n    // captured in the payload and flag the row as a guest\n    const recent = many(`\n      SELECT a.ts,\n             COALESCE(NULLIF(a.username,''), json_extract(a.payload,'$.ident')) AS username,"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/DashboardPage.jsx",
          "lines": "152-156",
          "snippet": "<span className={styles.feedUser}>{e.username || 'guest'}</span>\n                    {e.actor_id\n                      ? <span className={styles.feedId}>{e.actor_id}</span>\n                      : e.guest ? <span className={styles.feedGuest}>not signed in</span> : null}"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/DashboardPage.jsx",
          "lines": "8-31",
          "snippet": "const ACTION_LABELS = {\n  'scan.create':            'Scanned a rack',\n  'scan.select_port':       'Located a port',\n...\nconst labelFor = (a) => ACTION_LABELS[a] || a;"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": true,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
      "_corrected": true,
      "_votes": 3,
      "_refuted": 0,
      "id": "OPS-005"
    },
    {
      "question": "What exactly does the Logs tab show, and how do I filter it?",
      "answer": "The Logs tab is a live view (it refreshes itself every 4 seconds) of what the RackTrack server has been recording \u2014 email delivery, errors, and web requests.\n\nAt the top are four counters: Total kept, Info, Warn and Error (Error also includes any fatal entries). Below them:\n\u2022 Four filter buttons \u2014 All, Info+, Warn+, Errors. These are \"this level and above\", so Warn+ also shows errors and fatals.\n\u2022 A search box: \"Search messages, URLs, errors\u2026\". Press Enter to apply it; once applied, a \u2715 clears it. It matches anywhere in the stored entry \u2014 the message, URL, event name, error text, and the rest of the raw log line \u2014 so it will also find things like a request id or a user id buried in the entry.\n\nEach row shows the clock time and age, a level badge, the message, and for web requests the method, address, status code and how long it took. Click any row to expand it and see the full raw entry plus its request id (useful for following one request through several lines).\n\nUnder the filters, a line tells you exactly what you are looking at, for example \"Showing 300 of 1,240 entries \u00b7 kept 7 days\" (300 is the most rows loaded at once; 7 days is the default retention). Next to that line is a \"Clear log\" button, which deletes every stored entry after a confirmation \u2014 it cannot be undone.",
      "symptoms": [
        "What is in the Logs tab",
        "How do I filter logs",
        "How do I search the log",
        "What does the request id mean"
      ],
      "rootCause": "LogsView renders stat tiles, level tabs (All/Info+/Warn+/Errors), a search form and a table of rows from /api/logs; expanding a row lazily fetches /api/logs/:id for the full JSON line including request_id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "6-12",
          "snippet": "// Levels the server persists, lowest\u2192highest. Picking one filters to that\n// level *and above* (warn also shows error + fatal), matching how you triage.\nconst LEVELS = [\n  { key: '',      label: 'All' },\n  { key: 'info',  label: 'Info+' },\n  { key: 'warn',  label: 'Warn+' },\n  { key: 'error', label: 'Errors' },\n];"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "210-235",
          "snippet": "<StatTile label=\"Total kept\" value={stats?.total} />\n        <StatTile label=\"Info\"  value={byLevel.info}  tone=\"info\" />\n        <StatTile label=\"Warn\"  value={byLevel.warn}  tone=\"warn\" />\n        <StatTile label=\"Error\" value={(byLevel.error || 0) + (byLevel.fatal || 0)} tone=\"error\" />\n...\n            placeholder=\"Search messages, URLs, errors\u2026\""
        },
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "238-243",
          "snippet": "Showing {logs.length}{total > logs.length ? ` of ${total}` : ''} entries\n          {q ? ` matching \u201c${q}\u201d` : ''}\n          {stats?.retentionDays ? ` \u00b7 kept ${stats.retentionDays} days` : ''}"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "190-196",
          "snippet": "where.push(`(msg LIKE @q ${E} OR url LIKE @q ${E} OR event LIKE @q ${E} OR err LIKE @q ${E} OR meta LIKE @q ${E})`);"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": true,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
      "_corrected": true,
      "_votes": 3,
