    {
      "question": "What does \"Clear log\" do? Can I get the entries back afterwards?",
      "answer": "\"Clear log\" (bottom-right of the count line on the Logs tab) permanently deletes every stored log entry so you can start fresh. It is not undoable.\n\nBefore anything happens you get a confirmation box: \"Delete all N stored log entries and start fresh? This cannot be undone.\" Click Cancel if you are unsure. While it runs the button reads \"Clearing\u2026\".\n\nWhat it does and does not touch:\n\u2022 Deletes: every row in the server's stored application log, including entries the level filter or search box is currently hiding \u2014 not just the ones on screen. The database file is compacted afterwards.\n\u2022 Does NOT touch: the Operations tab. The activity feed, error list, user and organization figures come from a separate audit record in a different database file and survive a clear.\n\u2022 The clear itself is recorded \u2014 an audit entry and a fresh log line naming who cleared it and how many entries were removed are written immediately, so the empty log will already have one line in it.\n\nIf the button is greyed out: it is disabled whenever the current view has no rows, so clear the level filter and the search box (back to \"All\") and it will become clickable again.\n\nThere is no restore. If you might need the entries, note or copy what you need first.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Clear log",
        "Deleted the logs by accident",
        "Can I undo Clear log",
        "Log is empty after clearing",
        "How do I start the log fresh"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The Clear log button POSTs /api/logs/clear, which calls logStore.clearAll() \u2014 an unconditional DELETE FROM app_logs followed by VACUUM, with no backup written. It then writes an audit entry (action 'logs.clear') and one new log line. The audit_log table backing the Operations tab is a different database and is untouched.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "183-197",
          "snippet": "// Wipe every stored log line. Destructive and not undoable, so confirm first.\n  const clearLogs = async () => {\n    const n = stats?.total ?? logs.length;\n    if (!window.confirm(`Delete all ${n} stored log entries and start fresh?\\n\\nThis cannot be undone.`)) return;\n    setClearing(true);\n    try {\n      const res = await authFetch(apiUrl('/api/logs/clear'), { method: 'POST' });"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "149-159",
          "snippet": "// Wipe every stored log line and reclaim the file space \u2014 \"start fresh\".\n// Done through the live connection (rather than deleting logs.db on disk)\n// so the running server keeps a valid handle and nothing is corrupted.\n// Returns how many rows were removed.\nfunction clearAll() {\n  if (!db) return 0;\n  const before = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) c FROM app_logs').get().c;\n  db.prepare('DELETE FROM app_logs').run();\n  try { db.exec('VACUUM'); } catch (_) { /* not fatal \u2014 space just isn't reclaimed */ }\n  return before;\n}"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/app.js",
          "lines": "1817-1827",
          "snippet": "// POST /api/logs/clear  \u2192 wipe every stored log line (\"start fresh\").\n// Same admin gate as reading them. Audited, and we log one line immediately\n// afterwards so the fresh log records who cleared it and when.\napp.post('/api/logs/clear', auth.requireAuth, (req, res) => {\n  if (!requireLogAdmin(req, res)) return;\n  try {\n    const removed = logStore.clearAll();\n    audit.log({ req, action: 'logs.clear', status: 'ok', payload: { removed } });\n    logger.info({ event: 'logs.cleared', removed, by: req.user?.username },"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "30-31",
          "snippet": "const DATA_DIR = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'data');\nconst DB_PATH = process.env.LOG_DB_PATH || path.join(DATA_DIR, 'logs.db');"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": false,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
      "_corrected": true,
      "_votes": 3,
      "_refuted": 0,
      "id": "OPS-007"
    },
    {
      "question": "The \"Clear log\" button is greyed out and I can't click it.",
      "answer": "The button is switched off in two situations:\n\n\u2022 There are no rows in the list right now. The list is filtered on the server, so this happens either because your level filter or search matched nothing, or because the log is genuinely empty (nothing logged yet, or you already cleared it). Set the level tab back to \"All\" and clear the search box using the \u2715 beside it. The button turns on again as soon as at least one entry is listed \u2014 if the log is truly empty it stays off until new activity is logged, which usually takes a few seconds since the console refreshes every 4 seconds while Live is on.\n\n\u2022 A clear is already running. The button reads \"Clearing\u2026\" and stays disabled until the server confirms the wipe finished.\n\nImportant: Clear log always deletes every stored log entry, not just the rows currently shown. Filtering to \"Errors\" and then clearing will still remove your info and warn entries as well. You will be asked to confirm first, and it cannot be undone.\n\nIf you can see the Logs tab at all but the button never enables, check you are on the Logs tab of the Operations Console rather than the audit feed. Access is limited to the platform owner and any accounts your deployment lists as log admins; other users see \"Admin access required to view logs.\" instead of the table.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Clear log button greyed out",
        "Clear log disabled",
        "Clearing\u2026 stuck"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The button's disabled prop is `clearing || !logs.length`, so an empty filtered result set (not just an empty store) disables it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/pages/LogsPage.jsx",
          "lines": "244-252",
          "snippet": "<button\n          type=\"button\"\n          className={styles.clearLogsBtn}\n          disabled={clearing || !logs.length}\n          onClick={clearLogs}\n          title=\"Delete every stored log entry and start fresh\"\n        >\n          {clearing ? 'Clearing\u2026' : 'Clear log'}\n        </button>"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": true,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
      "_corrected": true,
      "_votes": 3,
      "_refuted": 0,
      "id": "OPS-008"
    },
    {
      "question": "Old log entries have vanished on their own \u2014 I didn't clear anything.",
      "answer": "That is normal housekeeping, not data loss. The log keeps entries for 7 days by default, and also caps the total at 200,000 entries \u2014 whichever limit is reached first wins, and the oldest entries are dropped. The line under the filters tells you the current retention, e.g. \"\u00b7 kept 7 days\".\n\nThe tidy-up runs automatically as new entries arrive, and once again each time the server starts.\n\nIf you need a longer history, ask whoever runs the server: the retention window and the row cap are set by the LOG_RETENTION_DAYS and LOG_MAX_ROWS settings.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Old log entries disappeared",
        "Log only goes back a week",
        "Log history is short",
        "kept 7 days"
      ],
      "rootCause": "log-store prune() deletes rows older than RETENTION_DAYS (default 7) and trims the oldest rows above MAX_ROWS (default 200000); it runs every PRUNE_EVERY (1000) inserts and once at init().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "33-37",
          "snippet": "// Retention: drop anything older than this many days, and hard-cap total rows\n// so a log storm can't fill the disk. Whichever bites first wins.\nconst RETENTION_DAYS = parseInt(process.env.LOG_RETENTION_DAYS, 10) || 7;\nconst MAX_ROWS = parseInt(process.env.LOG_MAX_ROWS, 10) || 200000;\nconst PRUNE_EVERY = 1000;   // run prune once per this many inserts"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "131-145",
          "snippet": "function prune() {\n  if (!db) return;\n  try {\n    db.prepare(\n      `DELETE FROM app_logs WHERE ts < datetime('now', ?)`\n    ).run(`-${RETENTION_DAYS} days`);\n    // Row cap: if still over budget, drop the oldest surplus by id.\n    const n = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) c FROM app_logs').get().c;\n    if (n > MAX_ROWS) {"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/log-store.js",
          "lines": "80",
          "snippet": "prune(); // clear anything stale left from a previous run"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": false,
      "audience": "admin",
      "confidence": "certain",
      "domain": "ops",
