    {
      "question": "The log used to be full of \"GET /api/logs/stats 200\" and now I don't see the console's own requests at all. Which is right?",
      "answer": "The current behaviour is correct. The Operations Console refreshes itself constantly (the Logs tab every 4 seconds, the Operations tab every 5), and each of those refreshes used to be written into the log \u2014 so opening the Logs tab filled the log with nothing but itself and buried the real activity.\n\nThose self-monitoring addresses are now deliberately left out of the log, along with the health-check and version addresses and static files. They are still measured for performance metrics; they are just not written as log lines.\n\nSo: not seeing your own log-viewer traffic is expected, and everything else is unaffected.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Log full of GET /api/logs/stats 200",
        "Console requests missing from the log",
        "Log floods when I open the Logs tab",
        "I can't see /api/logs requests"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The pino-http autoLogging.ignore predicate excludes /metrics, /healthz, /api/health, /api/version, /api/logs*, /api/admin/dashboard*, /uploads/, /outputs/ and /assets/ from request logging while the metrics middleware still records them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/lib/observability.js",
          "lines": "188-202",
          "snippet": "// This deliberately includes the endpoints the Operations Console polls to\n  // DISPLAY this log: /api/logs* refreshes every 4s and /api/admin/dashboard\n  // every 5s, so without this the log fills with nothing but its own polling\n  // (\"GET /api/logs/stats 200\" over and over) and buries the real activity.\n  autoLogging: {\n    ignore: (req) => {\n      const u = req.url || '';\n      return u === '/metrics' || u === '/healthz' || u === '/api/health'\n          || u === '/api/version'\n          || u.startsWith('/api/logs')             // the log viewer reading the log\n          || u.startsWith('/api/admin/dashboard')  // the console's live polling"
