    {
      "question": "Why can't I find debug or trace lines in the Logs tab, even though they appear in the server's terminal output?",
      "answer": "Only info-level entries and above are stored for the Logs tab \u2014 info, warn, error and fatal. The SQLite log mirror is attached at `{ level: 'info' }`, so debug and trace lines are never handed to it, and the dashboard table isn't drowned in development noise.\n\nWhere the debug detail actually goes depends on how the server is running:\n\n- On a development server (NODE_ENV is not \"production\"), the logger level defaults to `debug`, so debug lines do appear in the server's console/stdout even though they are absent from the Logs tab. This is the usual cause of \"the terminal shows more than the Logs tab\".\n- On a production server, the logger level defaults to `info`, so debug lines are not emitted at all \u2014 not to the Logs tab and not to the console. To capture them you must restart the server with `LOG_LEVEL=debug`.\n- Trace lines are never emitted under either default; they require `LOG_LEVEL=trace`.\n\nSo if you need debug detail for an investigation, read it from the server's own console/stdout rather than the Logs tab \u2014 and on a production host, set LOG_LEVEL first, or there will be nothing to read.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Debug lines missing from the Logs tab",
        "Trace not shown in the log viewer",
        "Logs tab shows less than the terminal"
      ],
      "rootCause": "observability.js pushes the log-store stream into pino.multistream at { level: 'info' }, so sub-info levels are never handed to the SQLite mirror.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/lib/observability.js",
          "lines": "86-91",
          "snippet": "try {\n  const logStore = require('./log-store');\n  logStore.init();\n  // Persist info+ only \u2014 debug/trace (span start/end, etc.) stay console-only\n  // so the dashboard table isn't drowned in dev noise.\n  streams.push({ level: 'info', stream: logStore.stream });"
        }
      ],
      "userCanSelfFix": false,
