    {
      "question": "The Logs tab is completely empty and stays empty even though the server is clearly busy.",
      "answer": "Check the server's own console output at startup for either of these lines:\n\u2022 \"[o11y] log-store unavailable, dashboard persistence off: \u2026\"\n\u2022 \"[log-store] init failed, log dashboard disabled: \u2026\"\n\nIf you see one, the log database could not be opened (a missing or unwritable server/data directory, a permissions problem, or a corrupt logs.db). RackTrack deliberately keeps running with logging-to-console only rather than failing \u2014 but the Logs tab will have nothing to show until the underlying problem is fixed and the server is restarted.\n\nIf you do not see either line, check in this order:\n1. The level filter is not set to \"Errors\" (the tabs filter that level and above) and the search box is empty \u2014 clear it with the \u2715.\n2. Someone may have pressed \"Clear log\" on the Logs tab, which empties the stored rows; new lines appear as traffic arrives.\n3. Only info-level and above is mirrored to the database \u2014 debug/trace lines stay console-only by design, so a server logging solely at debug will show an empty table.",
