    {
      "question": "What is the Lab page and who can use it?",
      "answer": "Lab is the platform owner's view of the virtual EVE-NG test switches. Open it at /lab, or click \"Lab\" in the desktop sidebar \u2014 the link only appears for the platform owner. The page header reads \"Lab \u00b7 Owner-only \u00b7 EVE-NG switches\".\n\nIt shows each registered lab switch as a card with its name, its host (IP address or hostname) and a status badge, plus a one-line fleet summary such as \"2 switches \u00b7 1 live \u00b7 1 offline\". Selecting a card automatically runs the same full switch audit the live-switch Ports screen runs \u2014 identity, ports, PoE, VLANs, LLDP neighbours and the MAC table \u2014 and you can re-run it from the detail panel.\n\nAnyone who is not the platform owner sees only \"Restricted to platform owners.\" That is not a fault and cannot be granted to an Organization Admin.",
