    {
      "question": "How do I pick a switch in Lab and run an audit? Do I have to press a button?",
      "answer": "No button needed in the normal case. Click a switch card and the audit starts on its own \u2014 the first card is selected for you when the page opens, so a report usually just appears.\n\nWhile it runs, the card badge and the button both read \"Connecting\u2026\". If there is no earlier result the page shows \"Auditing <IP address> over SSH \u2014 identity, ports, PoE, VLANs, LLDP and the MAC table\u2026\"; if you are refreshing an existing result the timestamp line reads \"Refreshing\u2026\" instead.\n\nTwo cases do not audit automatically: a switch with polling disabled, and one the background poller currently cannot reach (shown as Offline). Those display the reason instead, and you press the button to force an attempt.\n\nOtherwise an audit runs automatically only once per switch. After that the result is remembered, so clicking back and forth between switches shows what you last saw, stamped \"Audit as of 3m ago \u00b7 live SSH pass, not polled\". For a fresh reading press \"Refresh audit\" (the button reads \"Run full audit\" if there is no result yet).\n\nThis is deliberate: these switches accept only one SSH session at a time, and re-auditing on every click would fight the background poller for it. Only one audit runs at a time across the whole page.",
      "symptoms": [
