    {
      "question": "A Lab switch says \"Poller can't reach it\" with an SSH error. How do I read that message?",
      "answer": "Audience should be \"owner\", not \"admin\" \u2014 the Lab (/lab and /api/lab/*) is gated by requireRole('owner'), and org admins see a refusal instead of the device list. Answer body is accurate as written; optionally open it with \"On the owner-only Lab page\u2026\" so a non-owner reader isn't sent hunting for a screen they cannot reach. One small wording tightening: the refused branch also fires on any error text merely containing \"refused\", not only literal ECONNREFUSED.",
      "symptoms": [
