      "answer": "That is deliberate. When the background poller already knows it can't reach a switch (the device has a recorded error), RackTrack skips the automatic audit: the SSH attempt would just hang for the full timeout every time you selected that card. Showing you the offline diagnosis immediately is more useful.\n\nThe same applies to a switch whose polling you have disabled.\n\nYou can still force an attempt by hand with the audit button in the detail panel \u2014 it reads \"Run full audit\" before the first audit and \"Refresh audit\" once a result has been cached. The exception is a disabled switch, where the button is greyed out with the tooltip \"Polling is disabled for this device\"; use \"Enable polling\" first.",
