    {
      "question": "The Lab VLANs tab and LLDP tab both say \"None\". Is the audit broken?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 the audit is working. Both tabs print a note explaining why they are empty, and on the lab switches both are expected.\n\n\u2022 VLANs \u2192 \"None. Expected on CoreSW \u2014 it runs the L3 IOL image, where interfaces are routed and there are no switchports to put in a VLAN.\" Note: this wording is fixed text shown whenever no VLANs come back, so it names CoreSW even if you selected a different lab device. Read it as the general explanation, not as a claim about which device you are looking at.\n\u2022 LLDP \u2192 \"None. IOS needs `lldp run` globally, and the IOL l2-ipbase image may not support LLDP at all \u2014 Cisco defaults to CDP.\" To get neighbours on a Cisco lab switch, enable `lldp run` on it \u2014 but the image may not support LLDP regardless.\n\nThe MAC tab, when empty, says \"No MAC entries returned\"; the Ports tab says \"No ports returned\". The audit tabs are Identity, Ports, VLANs, LLDP and MAC.\n\nScope: the Lab view is platform-owner only (/lab and /api/lab/* are gated by requireRole('owner')); organization admins cannot open it and will see \"Restricted to platform owners.\"",
