    {
      "question": "How often does RackTrack poll a switch in the background, and why was it changed from every minute?",
      "answer": "Once an hour by default. It used to be every 60 seconds, and that was actively harmful: these switches (TP-Link JetStream, Cisco IOL) accept only ONE SSH session, and they don't release it when the connection drops \u2014 only on an idle timeout. Polling every minute meant the poller held that single session most of the time, so a technician's manual probe or a Lab audit had to fight it for access, and a burst of retries could saturate the switch until it was rebooted.\n\nHourly is enough because the Ports page reads stored snapshots and renders the last known state either way; only drift detection and the Lab view care about poll freshness.\n\nWhen the poller does run, 4 switches are polled at once by default (overridable with PORT_POLL_CONCURRENCY), each command has a 15-second timeout, and a poll runs immediately at server startup so the first reading doesn't wait an hour. Startup also clears any stale per-device backoff so a previously wedged switch gets a clean attempt.\n\nAdmin caution: the interval is overridable with PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS, and server/.env.example still ships PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000. If that file was copied to .env as-is, the deployment is still polling every 60 seconds and will exhibit the session-contention problem. Remove or raise that line \u2014 check the running deployment's server/.env rather than assuming, since some installs already set it to 3600000.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Polling interval",
        "Poll every 60s",
        "Switch stops accepting SSH connections",
        "Manual probe fights the poller",
        "PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS"
      ],
      "rootCause": "DEFAULT_INTERVAL_MS is 3_600_000 (1h) in port_poller.js and app.js starts the poller with Number(process.env.PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS) || 3_600_000; server/.env.example line 46 still sets 60000, which would override the hourly default.",
