    {
      "question": "A Lab switch has been offline for a while and doesn't seem to be retried every hour. Is polling stuck?",
      "answer": "Polling is not stuck. After a failed poll the poller backs the switch off on purpose: server/lib/port_history_db.js records consecutive_failures and a backoff_until timestamp, and the wait doubles with each consecutive failure \u2014 60 seconds for the first failure, then 2 min, 4 min, and so on, capped at 30 minutes (overridable with PORT_POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_MS / PORT_POLL_BACKOFF_MAX_MS). Devices inside their backoff window are filtered out of the poll cycle by dueDevices().\n\nImportant: the poller now runs hourly (PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS, default 3,600,000 ms), and the maximum backoff is 30 minutes \u2014 shorter than the interval. So backoff on its own will almost never cause a switch to miss an hourly attempt. If a Lab switch genuinely hasn't been retried, check these first:\n\u2022 Polling disabled for that device \u2014 the Lab page shows a \"Polling disabled\" banner; the poller skips it entirely.\n\u2022 No SSH credentials for that host/vendor \u2014 the poller logs \"no SSH creds\", stamps last_polled_at and returns without entering the backoff ladder at all.\n\nThe failure count is visible in the Lab page banner: \"Poller can't reach it \u2014 3 failed attempts.\", followed by the raw SSH error.\n\nTwo things clear a backoff:\n\u2022 Restarting the server \u2014 port_poller.start() calls clearAllBackoff() on every boot, so each device gets a clean immediate attempt. This is what recovers a switch wedged by the server being killed mid-SSH-session.\n\u2022 The operator force-reset (POST /api/port-poller/reset, optionally with a deviceId) \u2014 clears the backoff and kicks off an immediate poll cycle without restarting the server or rebooting the switch.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Switch not being retried",
        "consecutive_failures",
        "backoff",
        "failed attempts",
        "Polling seems stuck on a dead switch"
      ],
      "rootCause": "recordPollFailure computes an exponential backoff window (BASE_BACKOFF_MS 60s doubling per failure, capped at MAX_BACKOFF_MS 30min) and dueDevices() filters on backoff_until; port_poller.start() calls clearAllBackoff() at boot, and forceReset() clears it on demand.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/lib/port_history_db.js",
          "lines": "206-216",
          "snippet": "// Failure-tracking knobs \u2014 exponential backoff capped at MAX_BACKOFF_MS\n// so a permanently-dead switch retries on a sane cadence (default 30min)\n// instead of every poll interval.\nconst BASE_BACKOFF_MS = Math.max(1000, Number(process.env.PORT_POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_MS) || 60_000);\nconst MAX_BACKOFF_MS  = Math.max(BASE_BACKOFF_MS, Number(process.env.PORT_POLL_BACKOFF_MAX_MS) || 30 * 60_000);\n\nfunction backoffMsFor(failures) {\n  // failures=1 \u2192 BASE, failures=2 \u2192 BASE*2, ... capped at MAX.\n  const exp = BASE_BACKOFF_MS * Math.pow(2, Math.max(0, failures - 1));\n  return Math.min(MAX_BACKOFF_MS, exp);\n}"
        },
