    {
      "question": "What do \"Disable polling\" and \"Enable polling\" do on a Lab switch?",
      "answer": "Note: the Lab is owner-only (platform staff). /api/lab/* is gated by requireRole('owner') and the page renders a refusal for anyone else, so org admins cannot use this control.\n\n\"Disable polling\" tells RackTrack to leave that switch alone entirely. The detail panel then shows: \"Polling disabled. The poller skips this device entirely, so its data goes stale and no drift is recorded. Enable it to resume.\"\n\nWhile it is disabled the switch shows the \"Disabled\" badge (which takes precedence over \"Offline\"), no background readings are taken, no port-change history is recorded for it, and the audit button is greyed out with the tooltip \"Polling is disabled for this device\". Click \"Enable polling\" to resume; the button toggles between the two labels.\n\nUse it when a lab node is intentionally down and you don't want it counted as offline or retried.\n\nIf the toggle fails, the message appears near the top of the device list as \"Device list stale \u2014 Could not disable <name>: \u2026\" or \"Device list stale \u2014 Could not enable <name>: \u2026\".",
