    {
      "question": "Lab says \"No lab devices registered.\" \u2014 how do I add a switch?",
      "answer": "That message means nothing has been registered in RackTrack's monitored-switch list yet. Lab is a view of that list; it does not discover switches by itself.\n\nSwitches are added by the platform owner via the lab device API \u2014 there is no add form in the Lab page. POST /api/lab/devices with a JSON body: host (required), ssh_port (optional, defaults to 22), vendor (optional, defaults to tplink) and label (optional). All /api/lab/* routes are owner-only.\n\nRules the server enforces, in order:\n\u2022 Host must be a bare IP address or plain hostname \u2014 no scheme, credentials, port, or characters beyond letters, digits, dots, dashes and underscores, and it must start and end alphanumerically. Otherwise: \"host must be a bare IP or hostname\" (400).\n\u2022 SSH port must be an integer 1\u201365535, else \"ssh_port must be 1-65535\" (400).\n\u2022 Vendor must be one that has a polling recipe \u2014 currently tplink and cisco-ios. Otherwise: \"vendor must be one of: tplink, cisco-ios\" (400). Unknown vendors are rejected at write time rather than accepted and then silently skipped by the poller.\n\u2022 Host is unique \u2014 a repeat returns 409 \"device already exists for host <ip>\".\n\nOn success the server returns 201 with the created device. Related routes: GET /api/lab/devices (list), PATCH /api/lab/devices/:id ({ enabled }), DELETE /api/lab/devices/:id.\n\nSSH credentials are not part of this call \u2014 they are configured separately and stored encrypted on the server.",
