    {
      "question": "I pressed \"Poll now\" repeatedly and got an error about a rate limit or a poll already in progress.",
      "answer": "There are three things that can make manual polling fail or appear to do nothing. Two return an error, one is silent.\n\n\u2022 Rate limit (HTTP 429) \u2014 a maximum of 5 manual polls per 60-second sliding window, counted per person per switch (keyed on your user ID, or your IP if unauthenticated). The 6th attempt within the window returns \"rate limit: max 5 manual polls per minute\". Wait a minute and try again; other users are unaffected by your limit.\n\n\u2022 Overlap (HTTP 409) \u2014 if a poll for that switch is already running you get \"poll already in progress for this device\". Wait for it to finish; there is nothing to fix.\n\n\u2022 Poll now returns success but nothing updates (HTTP 200, no error) \u2014 this is the case with no error message. If someone is probing that same switch by hand, the poller yields the host for 60 seconds and the manual poll is skipped silently while still reporting success. Two things start that 60-second yield window: opening the live-switch ports view, and running a Lab audit (owner-only) against that device. Note that pressing \"Poll now\" itself does NOT start a yield window. Wait a minute after the live view or Lab audit finishes, then poll again.\n\nAll three guards exist because these switches (TP-Link JetStream and similar small managed switches) accept only one SSH session at a time \u2014 a background poll landing mid-probe makes the switch drop both sessions.",
      "symptoms": [
