    {
      "question": "How do I create a RackTrack account?",
      "answer": "Tap \"Create an organization\" on the sign-in screen. You enter your Email, a Username (3\u201332 characters, letters, digits and . _ -), your Organization name (at least 2 characters), and a password, which you type twice. The password needs all five of: at least 8 characters, an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, a digit and a special character \u2014 the screen shows which one is still missing as you type. RackTrack emails you a 6-digit code \u2014 type it into the \"Almost there\" screen and tap Verify.\n\nImportant: signing up this way always creates a BRAND NEW organization, and it makes you that organization's Org Admin. It does not add you to a team that already exists \u2014 to join an existing team you need an invite link from your organization admin. The code expires after 1 minute; if it lapses, tap Resend on the code screen for a fresh one.\n\nAfter you verify, your new organization is not usable yet \u2014 it goes to the RackTrack platform owner for approval, and you land on the \"Waiting for approval\" screen until they approve it.",
