    {
      "question": "I want to join my company's existing RackTrack team, but signing up made a new organization instead. How do I join the real one?",
      "answer": "You cannot join an existing organization by signing up \u2014 self sign-up always creates a brand-new organization (which then has to wait for RackTrack approval, which is why you may be stuck on the \"waiting for approval\" screen). Joining an existing team always comes from someone already inside it.\n\nImportant first step: your sign-up already claimed your work email address, and RackTrack will not let an invite be created or accepted for an email that already has an account. So before anything else, ask your organization admin \u2014 or the RackTrack platform owner if the stray organization needs deleting too \u2014 to remove the account you just created. Until that is done, your admin will see \"Someone with that email already has an account\" when they try to invite you.\n\nOnce your stray account is gone, there are exactly two ways in:\n\n1. Ask your organization admin (or your site manager) to send you an invite link for the right Site. It looks like .../invite/<code>. The invite is tied to your email address and is single-use, expiring after 7 days. Opening it shows which organization and Site you are joining; you choose your own username and password, tap Join, and you land straight in the app on the correct Site. (A site manager can only invite you as a Member; an org admin can also make you a Site Manager.)\n2. Ask your admin to create your account directly and hand you the username and password. You then sign in normally.\n\nFor reference, the sign-in screen spells this out under \"How to get access\": \"Joining an existing team? Ask your organization admin for an invite link, or a username & password \u2014 new sign-ups can't join an existing organization on their own.\"",
