      "question": "I see \"Request not approved\" or \"Organization deactivated\" \u2014 what happened?",
      "answer": "Both messages mean the RackTrack platform owner has acted on your organization, and the app is blocked for everyone in it.\n\n\u2022 \"Request not approved\" \u2014 your request to create the organization was rejected. The screen says: \"If you think this is a mistake, please contact them.\" There is no re-apply button; you have to contact the platform owner directly.\n\u2022 \"Organization deactivated\" \u2014 your organization was switched off. The screen says it \"will come back automatically if they reactivate it.\"\n\nOn both screens the only button is \"Sign out\". In both cases the page keeps re-checking your status in the background every few seconds, so if the platform owner reactivates (or approves) the organization while you're sitting on the screen, you're taken straight into the app without signing out and back in.\n\nNobody inside the organization \u2014 including your own org admin \u2014 can undo either state. Only the RackTrack platform owner can.",
