    {
      "question": "My invite link says \"Invite unavailable\", \"This invite has expired\" or \"This invite has already been used\".",
      "answer": "Invite links are single-use and expire 7 days after they are created.\n\n\u2022 \"This invite has expired\" \u2014 more than 7 days passed. Ask the person who sent it (your owner, org admin or site manager) to create a new invite link for you.\n\u2022 \"This invite has already been used\" \u2014 someone (probably you, earlier) already completed it. If you already have an account, use the \"Go to sign in\" link on the page and sign in normally; if not, ask for a fresh link.\n\u2022 \"Invite not found\" \u2014 the link doesn't match any invite. This is almost always a broken link rather than an expiry: the code was cut short by an email or chat client wrapping the URL, or it was retyped by hand. Copy the full link again from the original message and paste it into the address bar before asking for a new one.\n\u2022 \"Could not load this invite.\" \u2014 the app couldn't reach the server at all. Check your connection and reload the page; the invite itself is probably fine.\n\u2022 \"An account already exists for this email\" / \"That username is taken\" \u2014 the email on the invite is already registered, or the username you chose is in use. Sign in with the account you already have, or pick a different username. Usernames must be 3\u201332 characters using letters, numbers, and . _ - only.\n\nWhen the invite is valid you'll see \"You're invited\" and \"Join <Organization> \u00b7 <Site> as Member\" (or \"as Site Manager\"). Your email is filled in and locked by the invite; you only choose a username and password, then press Join.",
