      "question": "I forgot my password. How do I reset it?",
      "answer": "On the sign-in screen tap \"Forgot password?\".\n\n1. Enter your email and tap \"Send reset code\". RackTrack emails you a 6-digit code.\n2. The code expires in 1 minute, so have your inbox open before you request it. Type the code and tap \"Verify code\". If nothing arrived, use the \"Resend\" link under \"Didn't get a code?\" to get a fresh one.\n3. You'll land on a \"Code verified\" screen with two options: \"Yes, change password\" to set a new one, or \"No, take me to the app\" to sign in straight away without changing it. Either way you end up signed in.\n4. If you chose to change it, enter the new password twice (there's a confirm field) and tap \"Reset password\".\n\nYour new password must be at least 8 characters and include one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, a digit and a special character.\n\nIf no email arrives: for security RackTrack always says the request went through, even when that address has no account. Double-check you typed the address you actually registered with, and check your spam folder.\n\nMessages you might see: \"Reset code has expired \u2014 request a new one\" means you took longer than a minute \u2014 start again. \"Incorrect reset code\" means the digits don't match. \"No pending reset for that email \u2014 request a new code\" means the code was already used or cleared \u2014 request a fresh one.",
