      "question": "My password keeps getting rejected. What are the rules?",
      "answer": "A RackTrack password must satisfy all five of these:\n\u2022 at least 8 characters\n\u2022 at least one uppercase letter\n\u2022 at least one lowercase letter\n\u2022 at least one digit\n\u2022 at least one special character (anything that isn't a letter or a digit)\n\nOn the sign-up screen and the reset-password screen, a strength meter tells you exactly which one is missing \u2014 e.g. \"Need a digit\" or \"Need a special char\" \u2014 and turns into \"\u2713 Strong password\" when all five pass. If you submit before all five pass, you'll see \"Password is too weak.\"\n\nThe server enforces the same five rules everywhere: sign-up, invite acceptance, password reset, and when an administrator creates your account or sets a new password for you.",
