      "answer": "There are two reasons \"Marketplace\" may not be in your menu.\n\n1. Your role. The Marketplace (buying and selling surplus gear, listings, orders, alerts, partner accounts) is restricted to organization admins and the RackTrack platform owner. If you are a member or a site manager, the Marketplace link is hidden and opening the address directly returns you to the home screen. Ask your organization admin to list or buy the gear on your behalf.\n\n2. The device you are on. The Marketplace link only appears in the sidebar, which RackTrack shows on a desktop or laptop browser and on an iPad in landscape. On a phone the bottom bar is HOME / SCAN / PROFILE only, so there is no Marketplace link there even if you are an organization admin. If you are an admin, open RackTrack on a computer or a landscape iPad and Marketplace will be in the left sidebar, under Data Sources.\n\nIf you are an organization admin on a computer and still do not see it, or you see an \"Insufficient permissions\" message, contact your platform owner to confirm your role and that your organization is approved and active.",
