    {
      "question": "Sign-in fails: \"Invalid username or password\" or \"Invalid organization or credentials\". What's the Organization box for?",
      "answer": "The \"Organization (optional)\" box on the sign-in screen can be left blank. Blank means RackTrack looks you up by username or email alone \u2014 that works for almost everyone. Fill it in only if you have been told to, or if the same username exists in more than one organization.\n\nThe two error messages mean different things:\n\u2022 \"Invalid username or password\" \u2014 you left Organization blank and the username/email + password combination didn't match. Check for typos and try your email address instead of your username.\n\u2022 \"Invalid organization or credentials\" \u2014 you typed something in the Organization box. Either that organization doesn't exist, or your account isn't in it, or the password is wrong. Try clearing the Organization box and signing in with just your username/email and password.\n\nIn that box you can type your organization's name or your Site's name, or the short name (slug) either one was given \u2014 matching is not case-sensitive.\n\nIf you are certain the password is right and still can't get in, note that a deactivated account shows a different message \u2014 \"This account has been deactivated. Contact your administrator.\" \u2014 so keep looking for typos only while you are seeing one of the two messages above.",
