    {
      "question": "How long does a sign-in last, and why was I suddenly signed out?",
      "answer": "A RackTrack sign-in lasts 30 days. After that you are asked to sign in again. Your session is stored on the device you signed in on, so signing in on your phone does not sign you in on a laptop.\n\nBefore the 30 days are up, you'll be signed out if:\n\u2022 an administrator deleted your account (\"User no longer exists\"), or\n\u2022 your organization is no longer active \u2014 if the platform owner deactivates or rejects your organization, your session stops working, or\n\u2022 the server rejects your session for any other reason \u2014 RackTrack notices this on the next request and returns you to the sign-in screen rather than leaving you on a half-broken page.\n\nNote that being deactivated as a user stops you signing in again, but does not end a session you are already in \u2014 that one runs until it expires.\n\nIf the server is simply unreachable (no signal in the datacenter), RackTrack deliberately keeps your session so you are not stranded on a login page that also cannot reach the server \u2014 just try again once you have connectivity.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Invalid or expired token",
        "User no longer exists",
        "Authentication required",
        "I got bounced back to the sign-in screen",
        "Signed out on my phone but still signed in on the laptop"
      ],
