    {
      "question": "What are the four roles and what can each one actually do? (admin reference)",
      "answer": "RackTrack has four roles in a hierarchy: Platform Owner \u2192 Org Admin \u2192 Site Manager \u2192 Member.\n\n\u2022 Owner (RackTrack staff, member IDs start OWN-) \u2014 belongs to no organization and is never blocked by organization status. Creates organizations and their first org admin, approves/rejects/deactivates/deletes organizations, sees every organization's Sites, members and scans, and is the only role that can use the Lab and the Operations Console data. (An org admin can navigate to the /dashboard page, but the console's data API is owner-only, so they see a refusal message instead of the console.) Owner accounts cannot be edited or removed by anyone.\n\u2022 Org Admin (ADM-) \u2014 manages exactly one organization. Creates Sites, adds members, mints invites, changes member roles between Member and Site Manager, moves members between Sites, sets passwords, deactivates and removes members, and configures the organization's data-source connections. Also gets the Marketplace. Sees every scan in every Site of the organization.\n\u2022 Site Manager (ADM-) \u2014 manages one Site. Can add and invite people, but only as plain Members \u2014 never other site managers or admins. On existing accounts they may change only the active/inactive status and the password, and only for plain members of their own Site; they cannot change someone's username, email, role or Site. Their own scan visibility is the same as a member's: their own scans only.\n\u2022 Member (USR-) \u2014 the field technician. Full access to scanning, results, ports, cables, topology, network view, drift, switch info, firmware, specifications, SFP advisor, CMDB registration, sharing, feedback and their own profile/history. No Connections, Marketplace, Operations Console or Lab.\n\nCross-cutting: any non-owner whose organization is not 'active' is held on the /pending screen and gets HTTP 403 from every API route except /api/auth/* (which stays open so the pending screen can notice the moment an owner approves).",
      "symptoms": [
        "What's the difference between org admin and site manager",
        "Who can invite people",
        "Can a site manager create another site manager",
        "What does each role see"
      ],
      "rootCause": "Role semantics defined in the users.role migration comment and enforced by requireRole / canManageOrg / canManageSite plus the client's AdminRoute.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/auth.js",
          "lines": "205-214",
          "snippet": "// Role governs what a user can do:\n  //   'owner'        \u2014 platform superadmin (creates orgs + org admins)\n  //   'org_admin'    \u2014 manages one organization (creates Sites + users)\n  //   'site_manager' \u2014 manages one Site (adds members, runs scans)\n  //   'member'       \u2014 regular user within a Site\n  _ensureColumn('users', 'role', \"role TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'member'\");"
        },
