    {
      "question": "As an admin, how do I add someone to my organization? (admin)",
      "answer": "Open Profile \u2192 \"Organization Dashboard\" (owners see \"Owner Dashboard\"), which opens the Organizations console. Owners first pick the organization; org admins go straight into their own.\n\nUnder Sites, each Site row has two buttons:\n\u2022 \"Invite\" \u2014 enter their email and pick a Role (Member or Site Manager), then \"Create invite link\". You get a link to send them: \"Send this link to <email>. It works once and expires in 7 days.\" They open it and set their own username and password.\n\u2022 \"+ Add member\" \u2014 you set their username, email and password yourself and hand the credentials over.\n\nEither way the person lands in that specific Site. If you are a Site Manager you can only create plain Members, not other Site Managers.\n\nBoth are blocked while the organization is still awaiting approval \u2014 the server replies \"Your organization is awaiting owner approval.\" If the email already has a RackTrack account, an invite is refused with \"Someone with that email already has an account\", and \"+ Add member\" with \"That email is already registered\".\n\nTo change someone later, find them in the People section and click the \u22ee button on their card (clicking their name just filters the scan list): Edit (username, email, role, Site, new password), Deactivate/Reactivate, or Remove. The \u22ee menu is not shown for the platform owner, and org admins can only be edited by the owner. Removing deletes the account but keeps their past scans (they show as \"\u2014\").",
      "symptoms": [
