      "question": "As an admin I get \"Cannot edit an owner account\", \"Only the owner can edit an organization admin\", or \"You cannot remove your own account\". (admin)",
      "answer": "These are the guard rails on member management (server/auth.js, PATCH and DELETE /api/orgs/:orgId/members/:memberId):\n\n\u2022 \"Cannot edit an owner account\" / \"Cannot remove an owner account\" \u2014 RackTrack platform owner accounts are untouchable from the org console, by anyone.\n\u2022 \"Only the owner can edit an organization admin\" / \"Only the owner can remove an organization admin\" \u2014 an org admin cannot edit or delete a fellow org admin. Ask RackTrack (the platform owner) to make that change.\n\u2022 \"You cannot remove your own account\" \u2014 you cannot delete yourself; have another admin do it.\n\u2022 \"Not your organization\" \u2014 you tried to act on an organization you don't administer.\n\u2022 \"Not a member of your site\" \u2014 as a site manager you tried to change someone who is not a plain member of your own Site.\n\u2022 \"Role must be member or site_manager\" \u2014 those are the only two roles assignable from the console; you cannot promote anyone to org admin or owner here. Note this message only appears for owners and org admins: a site manager's edit silently ignores username, email, role and site changes entirely (they can only toggle active status or set a password), so a site manager never sees this error.\n\nAlso note the console hides these controls: a member row only shows the \u22ee menu when the target is not an owner and not an org admin you lack rights over.",
