    {
      "question": "How is my company's data kept separate from other companies? (organization / Site separation)",
      "answer": "RackTrack is organised as Platform \u2192 Organization \u2192 Site \u2192 Users. \"Site\" is what you'd think of as a datacenter or location.\n\n\u2022 Scans and racks belong to a Site. You can only open racks your own Site has scanned; anything else comes back as \"Rack not found\", with no hint that it exists elsewhere.\n\u2022 Your organization admin can see across every Site in your organization, but never into another organization.\n\u2022 The corrections you submit with the \"wrong?\" control are shared across your whole Organization (that's what improves recognition for your colleagues), not with other companies.\n\u2022 Data-source connections (ServiceNow, NetBox, etc.) can be set up org-wide by your organization admin \u2014 configured once and used by everyone in the organization \u2014 and individual users can also hold their own personal connection profiles. Either way the stored credentials are encrypted and never shown again, not even to the admin who entered them.\n\nA quirk worth knowing: if two different companies photograph the same rack, the rack gets the same internal ID because the ID is derived from the image itself \u2014 but ownership is still recorded per Site, so neither company can see the other's scan.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Is my data visible to other customers",
        "What is a Site",
        "Can another organization see our racks",
        "Rack not found"
      ],
      "rootCause": "tenants table = Sites, each with organization_id; rack_owners is keyed (tenant_id, rack_id) and requireRackOwnership gates by req.user.tenant_id. Org connection secrets are AES-256-GCM and never returned.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/auth.js",
          "lines": "189-192",
          "snippet": "// \u2500\u2500 Organizations (parent of \"Sites\" = tenants) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n  // Hierarchy: Owner (platform) \u2192 Organization (+ Org Admin) \u2192 Site\n  // (a tenant row) \u2192 Users. Racks/scans are per-Site; active learning is\n  // shared across the whole Organization."
        },
