    {
      "question": "Every page in the app suddenly returns \"Your organization is awaiting approval\" even though I could use it yesterday.",
      "answer": "Your organization's status changed away from active \u2014 to pending, rejected or deactivated. RackTrack blocks the whole app for everyone in that organization the moment that happens: the server rejects every request with \"Your organization is awaiting approval\", and the app moves you to the waiting screen, which tells you which of the three states you are in.\n\nOnly the RackTrack platform owner can set it back to active. Nobody inside your organization \u2014 including your org admin \u2014 can override it, so contact the platform owner directly.\n\nLeave the app open on the waiting screen. It rechecks your account roughly every 12 seconds and lets you back in automatically once the organization is active again. Sign-in and account endpoints are the only ones still permitted while you are blocked, which is exactly what makes that automatic recheck possible.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Your organization is awaiting approval",
        "All API calls return 403",
        "Every screen bounces to /pending",
        "It worked yesterday"
      ],
      "rootCause": "requireAuth calls orgBlocked(user) for every route except /api/auth/*, returning 403 with org_status when organizations.status !== 'active' for a non-owner.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/auth.js",
          "lines": "488-497",
          "snippet": "// /api/auth/* is exempt because PendingApprovalPage polls /api/auth/me to\n    // notice the moment an owner approves. ...\n    if (!String(req.originalUrl || '').startsWith('/api/auth/') && orgBlocked(user)) {\n      return res.status(403).json({\n        error: 'Your organization is awaiting approval',\n        org_status: orgStatusOf(user),\n      });"
        },
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/auth.js",
          "lines": "509-514",
          "snippet": "function orgBlocked(user) {\n  if (!user) return false;\n  if (user.role === 'owner') return false;\n  if (!user.organization_id) return false;\n  return !isOrgActive(user.organization_id);\n}"
        },
