    {
      "question": "I locked my phone / switched apps while a scan was running, and when I came back I was on the upload screen. Did I lose the scan?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 the scan almost certainly finished on the server, and RackTrack will bring it back for you. When you start a scan the app saves a small marker on the phone before uploading. When you return to the app it shows a full-screen message \u2014 'Bringing your scan back\u2026' with 'We're finishing the analysis you started. This takes a moment.' \u2014 while it asks the server what happened. As soon as the server says the scan is done, it drops you straight on the results. It waits up to 45 seconds, checking about every 1.5 seconds. If those 45 seconds run out before the server answers, don't panic: reopen the app and it will try again, because the marker stays on the phone for 15 minutes. (If the server instead reports that the scan failed or that it has no record of it, the marker is cleared and the app stops retrying automatically.) After 15 minutes the marker expires and automatic recovery stops. If that happens, go to Profile \u2014 the finished scan is in your scan list there. As a last resort, upload the exact same photo again: RackTrack recognises the identical image and returns the same result without re-analysing.",
