      "question": "How long do I have to reopen the app before a lost scan can't be recovered automatically?",
      "answer": "About fifteen minutes, counted from when you started the scan. RackTrack leaves a marker on your phone when a scan begins, and that marker expires 15 minutes later; the server keeps its matching record of the in-flight scan for 15 minutes too. Reopen RackTrack (signed in) within that window and it recovers the scan automatically and takes you to its results. After that the automatic recovery stops \u2014 but the scan itself is not lost. It finished on the server and appears in your scan list on the Profile screen; open it from there.",
