      "answer": "That link points at a rack the server no longer has on disk \u2014 the scan folder was deleted, lost in a server rebuild or data reset, or cleaned up automatically, or the rack ID in the link is wrong. When you open a rack link, RackTrack asks the server for that scan; if the server says it doesn't exist, the app quietly removes it from your local Scan history and sends you to the Scan screen so you aren't stuck on a broken page. (If you'd simply been signed out you'd land on the login screen instead, and a link from a different Site or teammate is not the cause \u2014 those still open.) Check your Profile scan list for the rack; if it isn't there either, the scan is gone and you'll need to re-photograph the rack.",
