      "question": "I pressed the refresh (Poll now) button several times and now it stops working.",
      "answer": "You've hit the limit of 5 manual refreshes per minute for that switch (the limit is counted per person, per switch, so it isn't affected by other users). The limit exists because each refresh opens a real login session to the switch, and most switches only allow one session at a time - repeated refreshes compete with the automatic hourly poll and can lock everyone out. Note that the Poll now button does not display an error when this happens: it simply appears to do nothing, which is the normal sign that you have hit the limit. The same silent no-op occurs if a poll for that switch is already running. Wait up to a minute and press it again; the allowance frees up gradually as your earlier presses age past the 60-second mark. If it still appears to do nothing after a couple of minutes, the switch itself is likely unreachable rather than rate limited.",
