      "answer": "'Waiting for first poll\u2026' means RackTrack has no switch set up for monitoring \u2014 the drift screen has no monitored device to show you. It is not a loading spinner, so waiting longer won't help. Ask your administrator to add a switch for monitoring and save its credentials.\n\nIf you instead see the switch's name and status but the message 'No port data yet.', the switch is configured but RackTrack hasn't managed a successful reading yet \u2014 usually it isn't reachable on the network. In that case RackTrack backs off after each failed attempt, doubling the gap from 1 minute up to a maximum of 30 minutes between retries. Restarting the RackTrack server clears that back-off and retries every switch immediately.",
