    {
      "question": "Admin: why is the switch still being polled every minute after the hourly change?",
      "answer": "Because a value set in the environment overrides the built-in hourly default. server/app.js:8574 resolves the cadence as `Number(process.env.PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS) || 3_600_000`, so any positive numeric value in server/.env wins over the 1-hour default (server/lib/port_poller.js:40, DEFAULT_INTERVAL_MS = 3_600_000). Note the `||` is falsy-coalescing: 0, blank or non-numeric values fall back to hourly, so only a real number causes this.\n\nCheck server/.env first. In this repo it already reads PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 (line 50), which is correct \u2014 the comment sitting above it is stale and still says \"default would be 60s\", ignore it. The real exposure is server/.env.example line 46, which still ships PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=60000, so any deployment seeded by copying the example file polls every 60 seconds. That is exactly the behaviour the hourly change was meant to stop, and it will hold the switch's single SSH session most of the time \u2014 which is what surfaces as \"Lost the SSH session\" on manual probes and Lab audits.\n\nFix: in that deployment's server/.env, either set PORT_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=3600000 or delete the line entirely to inherit the 1-hour default, then restart the server. Also update server/.env.example to 3600000 (or comment the line out) so new deployments stop inheriting 60000.",
