    {
      "question": "I lost signal \u2014 will RackTrack sign me out?",
      "answer": "No. If the app can't reach the server it deliberately keeps you signed in, because bouncing you to the sign-in screen would be useless when that screen can't reach the server either. You can keep using the parts of the app that don't need the server, and your session is re-checked the next time you open or reload the app with the server reachable (and on any request that comes back rejected). You are only signed out if the server actively rejects your session \u2014 most commonly because the session has expired. Sessions last 30 days from when you signed in, so a long stretch offline in the field is fine. Note that if an administrator deactivates your account, you are not kicked out of an active session \u2014 the block takes effect the next time you try to sign in.",
