    {
      "question": "Everything in the phone app fails to load even though my phone has good signal. Nothing works at all.",
      "answer": "This usually means the app is pointed at a server address that no longer exists, rather than your phone being offline. Test builds of the RackTrack app (the TestFlight IPA and the shared APK) have the server's public web address compiled in at build time. On the standard Windows test setup the server is published through a temporary Cloudflare tunnel, which generates a brand-new random address every time the server is restarted \u2014 so an app built against yesterday's address keeps calling a host that is gone, and every screen fails. Quick check: if the web version works in a phone browser but the installed app doesn't, this is the cause. Ask your administrator for the current address (on the server it is written to current-url.txt each time start.ps1 runs) and for a rebuilt app pointed at it \u2014 they run update-apk-url.ps1 to update the address and rebuild the web bundle, then produce the new APK in Android Studio. Note this applies to tunnel-based test deployments; if your server is reached over a fixed LAN or public address instead, there is no current-url.txt and the cause is something else.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Every screen fails on the phone app but the browser version works",
        "Sign-in fails with no obvious error",
