      "question": "The rack shortcuts (Overview / Ports / Topology) disappeared from the sidebar after I refreshed the page.",
      "answer": "That's expected. On a wide screen (the sidebar layout, 1024px and up) the RACK section \u2014 Overview, Ports, Topology, Network, Switches and Drift \u2014 only appears once you're actually looking at a rack in that browser session. RackTrack keeps the rack in memory only; it is never saved to the browser, so an old rack from a previous visit can't linger in your navigation.\n\nWhat clears it:\n- Refreshing the page while you're somewhere other than the rack itself (Home, Profile, Scan, and so on).\n- Opening the Scan page to start a new scan.\n- Signing out or signing back in.\n- A brand-new tab, which starts with nothing remembered.\n\nNote that refreshing while you are on the rack's own page (a /results/... or /switch-info/... address) does not lose the shortcuts \u2014 the rack is read straight back out of the address bar. To get them back after they've gone, open the rack again from your scan history on Profile, or open a /results link directly.",
