      "question": "Admin: I activated a data source connection and the 'pulling fresh data' banner never goes away.",
      "answer": "Activating a **ServiceNow** connection kicks off a background re-poll of the incident inbox and CMDB records (other connection types \u2014 NetBox, SolarWinds, Spectrum, own SQL/REST \u2014 do not trigger this pull, so the banner should not appear for them). The app waits 1.5 seconds, then checks progress every 3 seconds, and stops waiting after 6 minutes, showing 'Stopped waiting after 6 minutes \u2014 check the server log for poll progress.' The server itself kills the poll after 5 minutes and reports a failure naming the instance: 'Poll timed out after 300s talking to <instance>.service-now.com. Open <instance>.service-now.com in a browser, sign in to confirm it's awake, then try again.' The usual cause is a sleeping ServiceNow developer instance. Wake it in a browser, then activate the connection again. You can navigate away while it runs \u2014 the job continues server-side.",
