    {
      "question": "Owner: how far back do the Operations Console logs go, and does 'Clear log' delete anything else?",
      "answer": "Logs are kept for 7 days, and no more than 200,000 lines total \u2014 whichever limit is reached first wins, so on a busy day you may have less than 7 days of history. (A server administrator can change both via the LOG_RETENTION_DAYS and LOG_MAX_ROWS settings.) Pruning runs automatically once per 1,000 new log lines, and once when the server starts. 'Clear log' in the Operations Console wipes every stored log line through the live database connection and then compacts the file to reclaim disk space; it does not touch scans, users, or drift history. The action is audited, and a line is written immediately afterwards so the fresh log records who cleared it and when. While the console's Live toggle is on, the dashboard refreshes every 5 seconds and the Logs tab every 4 seconds; those self-monitoring requests are excluded from the log so they no longer drown out real activity.",
