    {
      "question": "Owner: the Lab page shows a switch audit that's clearly old \u2014 why doesn't it refresh itself?",
      "answer": "By design. An audit is a live SSH session, and these lab switches allow only one session at a time \u2014 which the background poller also uses. So the Lab runs an audit once, the first time you select a device, and then shows that cached result with an 'audit <time> ago' stamp on the card (and 'Audit as of <time>' above the report) rather than re-running it every time you click back to the device. To force a fresh pass, use the button in the device header: it reads 'Refresh audit' when a result is already on screen, and 'Run full audit' when there isn't one. If a device is disabled, or already known to be unreachable (shown as 'Offline'), the automatic audit is skipped entirely so it doesn't hang waiting on a timeout \u2014 the offline explanation appears immediately and 'Run full audit' still lets you retry by hand. The device list itself refreshes every 15 seconds, and the 'as of' ages tick every 10 seconds without refetching. Note the cache lives in the page only: reloading the Lab clears it, so the next device you select is audited fresh.",
