    {
      "question": "Admin: how long is drift and port history kept before it's deleted?",
      "answer": "Port change events are kept for 30 days and port state snapshots for 90 days by default. Snapshot clean-up only removes superseded rows, so the most recent snapshot for every port is always preserved regardless of age; event clean-up has no such protection and deletes everything past the cutoff. A clean-up sweep runs once when the port poller starts (i.e. at server startup) and then every hour. Both windows are configurable through PORT_DRIFT_EVENT_DAYS and PORT_DRIFT_SNAPSHOT_DAYS in server/.env; values are clamped to a minimum of 1 day, and a value of 0 or a non-numeric value silently falls back to the default rather than disabling retention. If you need drift evidence retained longer for an audit, raise those values before the window expires \u2014 the sweep is a hard delete with no undo and no archive.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Drift timeline empty beyond a month",
        "Historical port states unavailable for an old incident",
        "port_poller retention: pruned N event(s), N snapshot(s) in the log"
      ],
      "rootCause": "port_poller DEFAULT_EVENT_DAYS = 30, DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT_DAYS = 90, DEFAULT_RETENTION_MS = 60 * 60_000; _retentionTick() calls portsDb.pruneOldEvents/pruneOldSnapshots at startup and on that interval.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/lib/port_poller.js",
          "lines": "42-44",
          "snippet": "const DEFAULT_RETENTION_MS   = 60 * 60_000;  // sweep every hour\nconst DEFAULT_EVENT_DAYS     = 30;\nconst DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT_DAYS  = 90;"
        },
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/server/lib/port_poller.js",
          "lines": "260-271",
          "snippet": "const eventDays    = Math.max(1, Number(process.env.PORT_DRIFT_EVENT_DAYS)    || DEFAULT_EVENT_DAYS);\n    const snapshotDays = Math.max(1, Number(process.env.PORT_DRIFT_SNAPSHOT_DAYS) || DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT_DAYS);\n    const e = portsDb.pruneOldEvents(eventDays);\n    const s = portsDb.pruneOldSnapshots(snapshotDays);"
        },
