    {
      "question": "The drift screen updates on its own \u2014 how often, and does that hammer the switch?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 the drift screen never touches the switch. It only re-reads what RackTrack has already saved. The port grid refreshes about every 15 seconds; when you open a single port, its details and change list refresh every 15 seconds and the timeline chart every 20 seconds. All of that is reading stored data, so it costs the switch nothing.\n\nThe switch itself is contacted only on the background pass, which runs once an hour, or when you trigger a poll by hand using the refresh icon next to the switch name (manual polls are capped at 5 per minute). So a screen that refreshes often is not the same as data that is fresh \u2014 check the \"Last poll\" timestamp on the switch panel, not how often the page redraws.\n\nOne thing that trips people up: if the port grid is empty, the screen currently shows a message saying \"The poller runs once per minute.\" That text is out of date \u2014 the real interval is one hour. Trust the \"Last poll\" timestamp, and if you need current state right now, trigger a manual poll.",
