    {
      "question": "My correction ('wrong?' feedback) didn't save \u2014 I got 'Could not save'.",
      "answer": "Corrections are sent to the server the moment you tap Yes or Submit. There is no offline queue or local buffer for them, so if the connection drops at that point the correction is not stored anywhere. You'll see an error under the prompt \u2014 usually 'Could not save', though it may instead show the specific network or server message (for example 'Failed to fetch' or 'Load failed'). The control stays on screen and retryable: if you tapped Yes it returns to the Yes/No prompt, and if you were submitting a correction it returns to the dropdown with your choice still selected. Nothing is queued for later, so don't leave the results screen expecting it to sync \u2014 re-submit the correction once you're back online.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Could not save",
        "Correction reverts after leaving the screen",
        "'wrong?' feedback not reflected on a later scan"
      ],
      "rootCause": "StandardFeedback posts directly and on failure just sets an error string and returns the form to its prior phase \u2014 there is no retry queue, no localStorage buffer, and no background flush.",
