      "question": "The app opened fine but every screen is blank or shows an error. Is my phone broken?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 this is almost never the phone. The RackTrack app on your phone is only the screen; all the real work (the AI that reads your rack photos, and the live switch reading) happens on a server on our side. If that server is off, or the app was built pointing at an address that has since changed, every screen fails at once even though the app itself launches normally. You may see \"Load failed\" on each screen.\n\nWhat to do: report it to racktrackteam@sprintpark.com rather than reinstalling. Mention that the app opens but all screens fail \u2014 that tells us to check the server and the address baked into your build. A reinstall of the same build will not help, because the server address is fixed when the app is built; only a new build pointed at the current address will fix it.\n\nOne related case worth knowing: if photo scanning works but only the live switch screens (Ports, Cables, Trace, Network) are empty, that is also on our side, not your phone \u2014 but it is usually a different cause. Those screens read the switch directly, so they also need switch credentials configured, the switch reachable on the network, and (for Network) a Netdisco server set up. Messages like \"The switch didn't respond\" or \"Lost the SSH session\" point at that rather than at the app being broken.",
      "symptoms": [
