    {
      "question": "The app was working last week and now nothing loads. Nobody changed anything on my phone.",
      "answer": "This is almost always a server-side problem, not a phone problem \u2014 you're right that nothing changed on your device.\n\nRackTrack's app talks to a backend server reached over a Cloudflare tunnel, and there are two things that can break that link:\n\n1. The server or tunnel is simply down. The app only works while the host machine, the RackTrack server and the tunnel are all running. This is the most common cause, and it's fixed by the RackTrack team restarting the server \u2014 no new app build needed. Once it's back up, your existing app works again.\n\n2. The server's address changed. The current deployment uses a temporary Cloudflare quick-tunnel, which is issued a brand-new random https://<random>.trycloudflare.com address every time it restarts. That address is compiled into the app you installed, so if the tunnel restarted, every installed copy stops reaching the server until a new build is issued.\n\nEither way, there is nothing to do on the phone \u2014 reinstalling the same build will not help, and neither will clearing data. Report it to racktrackteam@sprintpark.com and mention roughly when it stopped working. If it's case 1 you'll be back up as soon as the server is restarted; if it's case 2 a rebuilt app has to be pushed out (a new TestFlight build on iPhone, a new APK on Android).",
      "symptoms": [
        "worked yesterday, nothing loads today",
        "all requests fail",
        "no data on any screen after a period of working"
      ],
      "rootCause": "start.ps1 opens a `cloudflared tunnel --url` quick tunnel whose https://<random>.trycloudflare.com hostname changes on every restart, and that hostname is baked into the shipped bundle. The mobile build guard explicitly warns about this.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "start.ps1",
          "lines": "37-49",
          "snippet": "Start-Process \"$ProjectRoot\\cloudflared.exe\" -ArgumentList \"tunnel --url http://localhost:3001\" ...\nif ($content -match \"https://[a-z0-9-]+\\.trycloudflare\\.com\") { ... $url | Set-Content \"$ProjectRoot\\current-url.txt\" }"
        },
        {
          "file": "client/scripts/check-api-base.mjs",
          "lines": "16-20",
