    {
      "question": "The camera doesn't start when I try to scan \u2014 I just get \"Camera access denied\".",
      "answer": "RackTrack shows \"Camera access denied. Allow camera permission or use Upload.\" when it cannot open the camera. The most common cause is that the phone has not granted camera access \u2014 the permission prompt appears on first use and is easy to decline by accident.\n\nFix the permission:\n- iPhone/iPad: Settings \u2192 RackTrack \u2192 turn Camera on. Then reopen RackTrack and try Scan again.\n- Android: Settings \u2192 Apps \u2192 RackTrack \u2192 Permissions \u2192 Camera \u2192 Allow.\n\nIf the permission is already on and you still see the message, the camera is usually busy or unavailable rather than blocked. Close any other app or browser tab using the camera (video call, camera app), then reopen RackTrack. If you opened RackTrack from a plain http:// link rather than the installed app or an https:// address, the camera will not start at all \u2014 use the installed app.\n\nEither way you can still scan without the camera: on the Scan screen use the Upload tab (it is the tab RackTrack opens on) and pick a photo you have already taken.\n\nNote: a preview that stays black, or \"Starting camera\u2026\" that never finishes, is a different problem \u2014 the camera did open but the preview did not start. Leave the Scan screen and come back, or switch between the Camera and Upload tabs to restart it.",
