      "question": "What permissions does RackTrack ask for on my phone, and do I have to say yes?",
      "answer": "RackTrack asks for these, each with a plain reason shown in the prompt:\n\n- Camera \u2014 \"RackTrack uses your camera to scan and photograph your equipment racks.\" Required for the Camera tab on the Scan screen. Say yes, or scanning from the camera will not work (you can still use Upload).\n- Photos \u2014 \"RackTrack reads photos you select for offline rack analysis.\" Only needed when you pick an existing photo via Upload.\n- Saving to Photos \u2014 \"RackTrack saves annotated rack scans to your photo library when you choose to.\" Only when you deliberately save a result.\n- Microphone \u2014 \"RackTrack needs microphone access to record video scans of your rack.\" In practice the in-app video scan records picture only, so you should not normally see this prompt.\n\nOn Android the app additionally declares Internet and Camera. Everything else \u2014 no location, no contacts, no background tracking.",
