      "answer": "There are two hard limits on a rack scan upload:\n\n- Size: 340 MB per file. A long 4K video will exceed this \u2014 record a shorter clip or drop the recording quality.\n- Type: the file must be a recognised photo or video. Accepted extensions are jpg, jpeg, jfif, png, gif, webp, tif, tiff, avif, bmp, heic, heif for photos, and mp4, mov, webm, m4v, avi for video. Anything else is refused with \"Invalid file type\" (in the app you may see \"Unsupported file type. Upload an image or video.\"). For video, stick to mp4, mov or webm \u2014 these are the formats the frame extractor handles.\n\niPhone HEIC photos are fine \u2014 RackTrack converts them to JPEG on the server and applies EXIF rotation.\n\nNote: marketplace listing photos are a separate, stricter upload \u2014 8 MB maximum, and only jpg, png, webp or heic. That one fails with \"Only jpg / png / webp / heic images are accepted\".",
