      "answer": "RackTrack accepts up to 20 scan uploads per minute. Scanning a whole row back to back can hit that ceiling.\n\nWhat to do: the message tells you how long to wait \u2014 wait that many seconds and scan again. The allowance refills continuously, so it is usually only a few seconds before you can shoot the next rack, not a full minute.\n\nThe scan you were trying to send was not accepted, so re-take or re-submit that one. Everything you scanned before it is safe and already saved \u2014 nothing you have already captured is lost.\n\nOne thing to know: for scan uploads this allowance is shared by everyone connecting from the same network, not tracked per person. If several technicians on the same site network are scanning at once, you can hit the limit sooner than you expect. Switching to a different phone on the same network will not give you a fresh allowance; pausing for a few seconds will.",
