      "answer": "No. RackTrack keeps a ticket for the scan that was running. When you come back (or reopen the app), it shows a full-screen \"Bringing your scan back\u2026\" spinner with the note \"We're finishing the analysis you started. This takes a moment.\", then drops you straight on the finished results.\n\nIt waits up to about 45 seconds for the scan to finish. If it is still not ready by then, the spinner clears and you stay where you are \u2014 reopen the app a moment later and it will try again; the analysis keeps running on the server regardless. The ticket is kept for 15 minutes, so if you leave it much longer, open the scan from your history in Profile instead. If the scan failed on the server, the spinner simply clears and you are left on the screen you were on.",
