      "answer": "Admin/internal. This is the ngrok interstitial bug. A free ngrok tunnel serves a ~2.8 KB HTML warning page (with HTTP 200) instead of the real bytes to any client whose user-agent looks like a browser \u2014 and a Capacitor WebView does.\n\nTwo separate fixes are required and both must be present in the shipped build:\n\n1. The fetch interceptor (client/src/main.jsx calls installFetchInterceptor() from client/src/utils/api.js) adds the `ngrok-skip-browser-warning: true` header. This fixes API calls only.\n2. The `overrideUserAgent` keys in client/capacitor.config.json fix images. `<img>` tags cannot send custom headers, so no JavaScript can rescue them \u2014 without the override every scan result image, overlay and rack photo renders broken.\n\nBoth are currently present in the repo. If a build regresses, verify on a phone: the result image rendering is the check that catches it (MAC-IPA-SETUP.md Step 6).",
