      "question": "How do I ship a new build to testers, and what stops a build from being accepted?",
      "answer": "Admin/internal.\n\niOS (Mac only \u2014 Xcode does not run on Windows):\n1. Bump CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION in client/ios/App/App.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj (both occurrences \u2014 the file has exactly two). TestFlight rejects a duplicate build number outright. Leave MARKETING_VERSION = 1.0 alone. (Note: MAC-IPA-SETUP.md's \"you are on 1.0 (4)\" example is stale \u2014 read the current value out of the file.)\n2. `cd client && npx cap sync ios`\n3. `./make-ipa.sh <TEAM_ID> https://<backend>` \u2014 e.g. `./make-ipa.sh 6GS882NNAX https://\u2026`. The API URL argument is optional: if omitted, make-ipa.sh falls back to the tunnel URL in /tmp/cf_url.txt, and only fails with \"\u2716 no API url (pass one, or start the tunnel)\" when neither is available. Whatever URL it ends up with is passed to `npm run build:mobile`, which runs client/scripts/check-api-base.mjs first \u2014 that hard-fails with \"\u2716 Mobile build blocked:\" on an empty, localhost/127.0.0.1/0.0.0.0, or non-HTTPS value, and warns (does not fail) on a trycloudflare.com quick tunnel because its URL changes on every restart. Output lands in client/build/ipa/App.ipa.\n4. `./ship-ipa.sh \"\u2022 release notes\"` \u2014 release notes are mandatory (it prints usage and exits without them). It uploads via `xcrun altool` using an App Store Connect API key and then sets the TestFlight \"What to Test\" text via testflight-notes.mjs. Apple processing is usually 5\u201330 minutes; nobody can install until it clears.\n\nAndroid:\n`./ship-apk.sh \"release notes\"` builds the web bundle with VITE_API_BASE baked in (falling back to a hardcoded ngrok backend if the env var is unset), runs `npx cap copy android` then `gradlew assembleDebug`, and pushes the APK to the Firebase App Distribution \"testers\" group (override with FIREBASE_GROUP). Needs `firebase login` and a Firebase Android App ID in client/.firebase-app-id or FIREBASE_APP_ID. Testers get an email plus a push in the App Tester app. Android can also be built on Windows; iOS cannot.\n\nCommon blockers: duplicate build number; VITE_API_BASE empty/localhost/http (iOS path); missing AuthKey_<KEY_ID>.p8 (default AuthKey_ZGYSK2PGM4.p8) in ~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys or the repo root; firebase CLI missing or not logged in; no Firebase App ID.",
