      "answer": "Internal. The phone never touches the switch \u2014 the server does. Every live feature depends on the backend host being able to reach the equipment's private LAN; no client-side change affects this.\n\nWorks on any internet connection (assuming a hosted HTTPS backend exists): sign in/sign up, scan (photo, multi-image stitch, video), AI detection, results/overview, port location from the photo, specifications, firmware lookup, SFP advisor, reports, share, marketplace, profile/history.\n\nWill NOT work for a remote tester on a cloud backend: Live switch Ports tab, Cables view, Trace tab, Drift polling, switch console \u2014 all need server\u2192switch SSH on the private LAN (e.g. 192.168.1.x) \u2014 and the Netdisco Network view, which needs the backend to reach the Netdisco discovery server on that same LAN (HTTP, not SSH).\n\nDo not triage these as app or install problems. The tell is: photo scanning works fine but only the live screens are empty. Beta workaround is a backend on a machine with LAN/VPN access to the switch, exposed via an HTTPS tunnel; the production answer is an on-prem collector.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Ports tab empty for a remote tester",
        "The switch didn't respond",
        "Network view never loads",
        "Drift stuck on Waiting for first poll\u2026",
        "live screens empty while scanning works"
