      "question": "The sign-in screen just says \"rate_limited\" \u2014 what does that mean and how long do I wait?",
      "answer": "You tried to sign in too many times in a short burst, so RackTrack temporarily throttled attempts for your account.\n\nWhat's happening: the server allows 20 attempts back-to-back, then refills at 10 attempts per minute \u2014 roughly one attempt every 6 seconds. The error message may say \"Too many uploads \u2014 retry in 6s\"; ignore the word \"uploads\", the same throttle code is reused for sign-in.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Wait about 10 seconds and try once more. Extra taps while you're throttled are simply rejected \u2014 they don't make the wait longer \u2014 but they won't get you in either, so just wait.\n2. If you're not sure of your password, stop guessing and use \"Forgot password?\" instead.\n3. This is per-account, not per-device. Your colleagues can still sign in normally, and switching to another phone or Wi-Fi will not clear it \u2014 only waiting does.\n\nGood news: your account is NOT locked. RackTrack has no lockout requiring an administrator to unlock you. The throttle clears on its own.",
