      "answer": "Your individual user account was switched off by an administrator. Your password is fine; the server checks your password first, then refuses the sign-in on purpose (HTTP 403).\n\nImportant: nothing you do on the phone will fix this. Resetting your password, reinstalling the app, or trying a different device will all produce the same message.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Contact your organization admin. (A site manager can also do this, but only for regular members in their own Site \u2014 if you are a site manager or an admin yourself, you need an organization admin or the platform owner.)\n2. Ask them to open the Organizations console, find you in the Members list, open the menu on your row and choose \"Reactivate\".\n3. Then sign in normally \u2014 no new password needed. Your past scans and history are still there; deactivation never deletes them.\n\nIf your admin says your account looks active, ask them whether the whole ORGANIZATION was deactivated instead. That is a different problem: your sign-in actually succeeds, and you land on a screen titled \"Organization deactivated\". Only the RackTrack platform owner can reverse that one.",
