      "answer": "Your sign-in worked. What's blocking you is that your organization has not been approved yet.\n\nWhen you create an organization by signing up, RackTrack files it as a request. A RackTrack platform owner has to approve it before anyone in it can scan racks or use the rest of the app.\n\nWhat you'll see: a screen titled \"Waiting for approval\" with the text \"Your request to create <your organization> has been sent to the platform owner.\" The page re-checks by itself every few seconds, and there's a \"Check now\" button if you're impatient.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Contact the RackTrack platform owner directly (by phone/email/chat). They are NOT emailed automatically when you sign up \u2014 if nobody tells them, nobody approves you.\n2. Leave the app open, or come back later; the moment they approve, the screen moves you straight into the Scan page. You do not need to sign in again.\n3. If you were meant to join a team that already exists, you signed up the wrong way \u2014 see the entry about invite links.\n\nTwo related screens use the same page:\n- \"Request not approved\" \u2014 the owner rejected the request.\n- \"Organization deactivated\" \u2014 the owner switched your whole organization off. It comes back automatically if they reactivate it.",
