      "question": "How long does my sign-in last? Why was I suddenly asked to sign in again?",
      "answer": "A RackTrack sign-in lasts 30 days. After that the app signs you out and shows the Sign in screen again. That's normal and expected \u2014 just sign in again.\n\nRackTrack does not silently renew your session in the background: there is no refresh step. The 30 days start when you sign in and don't get extended by using the app, so even a technician who scans racks daily will be asked to sign in roughly once a month.\n\nYou will ALSO be signed out immediately (before the 30 days) if:\n- An administrator deleted your account. The app sees \"User no longer exists\".\n- The RackTrack server was reinstalled or its signing key was replaced (ask your admin).\n- You cleared your browser's site data, used a private/incognito window, or cleared the app's storage on the phone.\n\nWhat you will NOT be signed out by:\n- Closing the app, switching to another app, or restarting your phone.\n- Losing signal. Going offline keeps you signed in on purpose.\n- Changing your own password (existing sessions keep working).",
