    {
      "question": "The Sign in screen shows something like \"Load failed\" or \"Failed to fetch\" instead of an error about my password.",
      "answer": "That is not a password problem. Your device could not reach the RackTrack server at all, so it never got as far as checking your credentials.\n\nHow to tell the two apart:\n- \"Invalid username or password\" \u2014 or \"Invalid organization or credentials\" if you filled in the optional Organization field \u2014 means the server answered and rejected you. Fix your credentials (and check the Organization name, since a wrong org name produces the same message as a wrong password).\n- \"This account has been deactivated. Contact your administrator.\" also means the server answered \u2014 that is an account state, not a network fault.\n- \"Load failed\", \"Failed to fetch\", \"NetworkError\", or \"Request failed (502/503/504)\" = the server did not answer. Your credentials were never tested.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Check you actually have signal or Wi-Fi. Open any website in your phone browser to confirm.\n2. If you're in a datacenter, you may be on a restricted network. Switch to mobile data and try again \u2014 this is by far the most common cause in the field.\n3. If you're on a corporate VPN or guest Wi-Fi that blocks unknown sites, get off it or ask your network team to allow the RackTrack address.\n4. If everyone at your site is affected at the same time, the RackTrack server or its public address is down \u2014 contact your administrator rather than retrying.\n\nWhile you're offline you cannot sign in for the first time \u2014 RackTrack has no offline sign-in. If you were already signed in, the app deliberately keeps you signed in when the server is unreachable, so you won't be thrown out to the login screen while out of coverage. You are only signed out if the server explicitly rejects your session.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Load failed",
        "Failed to fetch",
        "Request failed (502)",
        "Request failed (503)",
        "Error text on Sign in that doesn't mention the password",
        "Spinner then a red bar with a browser-style message"
      ],
      "rootCause": "AuthContext.callApi does a bare fetch; a transport failure rejects with the browser's own TypeError (WebKit: 'Load failed', Chromium: 'Failed to fetch') and LoginPage renders err.message verbatim in the error box. Non-JSON/gateway responses fall through to `Request failed (${res.status})`. There is no offline credential store \u2014 login always requires a live round-trip.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "/Volumes/Racktrack/dark_mobile/client/src/AuthContext.jsx",
          "lines": "18-28",
          "snippet": "async function callApi(path, options = {}) {\n  const res = await fetch(apiUrl(path), { method: 'POST', ... });\n  let data = {};\n  try { data = await res.json(); } catch { /* non-JSON response */ }\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.error || `Request failed (${res.status})`);"
        },
