      "question": "The verification code from my signup email says it's expired, and now \"Resend\" says there's no pending signup.",
      "answer": "The 6-digit code you get when creating an account is only valid for 1 minute. The email says so: \"It expires in 1 minute.\"\n\nThere's a trap worth knowing: if you tap \"Verify\" AFTER the minute has passed, RackTrack throws away your half-finished signup entirely. You'll see \"Verification code has expired \u2014 sign up again\", and if you then press \"Resend\" you get \"No pending signup for that email\" \u2014 because there's nothing left to resend to.\n\nWhat to do:\n\n- If it just expired: tap the back arrow at the top left to return to the signup form. Your details are still filled in \u2014 just press the signup button again to get a fresh code. No account was created, so nothing conflicts and you can reuse the same email.\n- If you're still waiting on the email and haven't submitted a code yet: press \"Resend\" (under \"Didn't get it?\"). That works and gives you a fresh minute.\n- Check your spam/junk folder first \u2014 the mail comes from your organization's RackTrack sending address.\n\nTo avoid it next time: open your email app first, then start the signup, so the code is waiting for you. The code boxes support your phone's one-time-code autofill, so if your keyboard offers the code as a suggestion, tap it instead of switching apps. If the code doesn't appear that way, just read it and type it \u2014 you have a full minute from when the email is sent.",
