      "answer": "The Forgot password screen always shows the same message \u2014 \"If an account exists for that email, a 6-digit code is on its way.\" \u2014 whether or not the email is registered. That's deliberate privacy protection, but it means a missing code has several possible causes:\n\n1. That email address has no RackTrack account. Very common if you signed up with a work address but typed your personal one, or if your admin created your account under a different address. Ask your admin which email is on your account.\n2. The code went to spam/junk.\n3. The RackTrack server's outgoing email isn't working. Unlike signup, the Forgot password screen does NOT warn you when the email fails to send \u2014 it reports success either way.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Check spam/junk, and search your mail for \"RackTrack verification code\".\n2. Try again with any other email address you might have used.\n3. Remember the code only lasts 1 minute \u2014 if it arrives slowly, tap \"Resend\" on the code screen and use the newest one.\n4. If nothing arrives on any address, contact your organization admin. They can set a new password for you directly from the Members list, which bypasses email completely.",
