    {
      "question": "What exactly does the password reset flow do, and can I get in without changing my password?",
      "answer": "Yes. The reset flow has four steps and you can stop after step three:\n\n1. \"Forgot password\" \u2014 enter your email, tap \"Send reset code\".\n2. \"Enter code\" \u2014 type the 6-digit code. It expires in 1 minute; there's a \"Resend\" link. Checking the code here does NOT use it up.\n3. \"Code verified\" \u2014 RackTrack asks \"Change your password? You're signed in either way.\"\n   - Tap \"No, take me to the app\" and you're signed in with your existing password unchanged.\n   - Tap \"Yes, change password\" to continue.\n4. \"New password\" \u2014 type it twice. The strength bar must be full.\n\nEither way you end up signed in immediately (a 30-day session) \u2014 no second trip to the Sign in screen.\n\nYour new password must have at least 8 characters, one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one digit, and one special character. If any are missing the screen tells you which one (for example \"Password must contain a special character\") or shows \"Password is too weak.\"\n\nOne caution: the code is single-use once you finish \u2014 BOTH finishing paths use it up, including \"No, take me to the app\". If you back out of the screen after step 3 without tapping either button, request a fresh code.\n\n(Internal note for the rootCause field: /verify-reset-code returns only { ok: true } and no token; only /login-with-code and /reset-password issue the fresh 30-day token.)",
      "symptoms": [
        "Code verified",
        "Change your password? You're signed in either way.",
        "Password is too weak.",
        "Passwords do not match.",
        "Password must contain a special character",
        "Reset code has expired \u2014 request a new one",
        "Incorrect reset code"
      ],
      "rootCause": "Three-endpoint reset: /verify-reset-code checks without deleting the password_resets row; /login-with-code issues a token and consumes the row without touching password_hash; /reset-password validates against validatePassword(), rehashes with bcrypt and consumes the row. All three return a fresh 30-day token.",
      "evidence": [
