    {
      "question": "Is there Single Sign-On, Microsoft/Google login, or two-factor authentication?",
      "answer": "No. RackTrack has exactly two ways to sign in:\n\n1. Username or email + password on the Sign in screen. (The screen also has an \"Organization\" field \u2014 it is optional. Leave it blank unless your admin told you otherwise; it only matters when the same username exists in more than one organization.)\n2. A one-time 6-digit code emailed to you via \"Forgot password?\" \u2014 after you enter the code you're asked \"Want to change your password?\", and choosing \"No, take me to the app\" signs you in without changing it.\n\nThere is no \"Sign in with Microsoft\", no \"Sign in with Google\", no SAML/SSO, and no authenticator-app or SMS two-factor step. If someone told you to look for an SSO button, they're thinking of a different system.\n\nTwo things that look like SSO but aren't:\n- The 6-digit codes at signup and password reset are email verification, not two-factor. They never appear on a normal sign-in.\n- On the Firmware and Switch screens, RackTrack links out to switch vendors' own login pages (Cisco, Juniper, etc.). Those are the vendors' logins, not RackTrack's.\n\nSo if you've lost your password, the email reset code is the only self-service route back in. Otherwise your organization admin can set a new password for you \u2014 and if you're a regular member, your site manager can do it too.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Looking for an SSO or 'Sign in with\u2026' button that doesn't exist",
        "Expecting an authenticator-app prompt after entering the password",
        "Asked to configure MFA"
      ],
      "rootCause": "The auth surface exposed by AuthContext is login / signup / verifyCode / resendCode / forgotPassword / verifyResetCode / resetPassword / loginWithCode. No OIDC/SAML/TOTP dependency or route exists; the only OAuth in the codebase is eBay/Amazon marketplace seller linking, and the only SSO URLs are outbound vendor links.",
