    {
      "question": "My colleague sent me an invite link but it says the invite has expired / has already been used.",
      "answer": "Invite links are single-use and last 7 days. Once someone completes the sign-up form on that link it's dead; after a week an untouched link dies too.\n\nWhat you may see on the invite page:\n- \"This invite has expired\" \u2014 more than 7 days have passed since it was created.\n- \"This invite has already been used\" \u2014 an account was already created from it.\n- \"Invite not found\" \u2014 the link was mistyped or truncated by a chat app, so the code doesn't match any invite. Copy the whole link rather than typing it.\n- \"An account already exists for this email\" \u2014 you already have a RackTrack account on that address. Go to Sign in and use \"Forgot password?\" instead. (Usually your admin will hit this first: RackTrack refuses to issue an invite to an email that already has an account.)\n- \"That username is taken\" \u2014 pick a different username; usernames must be unique across all of RackTrack.\n- \"Could not load this invite.\" \u2014 that's a network problem, not a bad invite. Check your connection and reopen the link.\n\nSteps to fix: ask whoever invited you (your organization admin or site manager) to generate a new invite for your email address. There's no way to revive an old one.\n\nNote: accepting an invite signs you in immediately and drops you on the Scan screen \u2014 you set your own username and password, and you do not need approval from the platform owner.",
      "symptoms": [
        "This invite has expired",
        "This invite has already been used",
        "Invite not found",
        "This invite is invalid.",
        "Could not load this invite.",
        "An account already exists for this email",
        "Could not accept the invite."
      ],
      "rootCause": "invites.expires_at = Date.now() + 7*24*60*60*1000 and accepted_at is stamped on first use; both GET /api/invites/:code and POST /api/invites/:code/accept return 410 on used/expired and 404 on unknown codes. AcceptInvitePage renders the server's error string, or 'Could not load this invite.' for a fetch rejection.",
      "evidence": [
