    {
      "question": "I want to join my company's existing RackTrack team, but signing up created a brand-new organization stuck waiting for approval.",
      "answer": "That's the expected behaviour, and it's the single most common first-time setup mistake. \"Create an organization\" on the Sign in screen is for setting up a NEW team. New sign-ups can never join an existing organization on their own \u2014 once you enter the emailed verification code, signup always creates a fresh organization (named after the company name you typed) plus a \"Main Site\", makes you its admin, and files it as pending for platform-owner approval.\n\nThe Sign in screen actually spells this out under \"How to get access\":\n- \"Setting up your own team? Tap Create an organization above.\"\n- \"Joining an existing team? Ask your organization admin for an invite link, or a username & password \u2014 new sign-ups can't join an existing organization on their own.\"\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Ask your organization admin (or site manager) for either an invite link or a username and password they create for you.\n2. If you already went through signup by mistake, don't wait on the approval screen \u2014 that organization is a dead end for you. Let your admin or the RackTrack platform owner know so they can reject or delete it; it won't disappear on its own.\n3. Open the invite link, confirm the pre-filled email, choose a username and create a password, and you're straight into your team's site.",
      "symptoms": [
