      "answer": "This message means RackTrack itself could not hand your verification email to a mail server. It is a server-side problem, not something wrong with your address or your phone. You will see it on both the signup step and when you tap \"Resend\".\n\nWhat NOT to do: retrying repeatedly won't help if the mail account is misconfigured \u2014 RackTrack already tries every configured mail provider (including the backup one, if your administrator set one up) before showing you this error. After about 20 rapid signup attempts you'll also hit the sign-up throttle.\n\nSteps to fix:\n1. Wait a minute and try once \u2014 brief mail-provider hiccups do clear.\n2. If it persists, this needs your RackTrack administrator: the server's outgoing mail settings (SMTP) are broken, the mail password has expired, or no mail server is configured at all.\n3. In the meantime, ask your organization admin to create your account directly from the Organizations console, or send you an invite link \u2014 both paths mark your email as verified automatically and skip the code entirely, so you can start working today.",
