    {
      "question": "I'm signed in fine but the Operations Console / Lab / Integrations / Marketplace tells me I'm not allowed. Is my login broken?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 your sign-in is working. Those screens are limited by role, and RackTrack keeps you signed in rather than sending you back to the Sign in screen.\n\nWho can reach what:\n- Operations Console (/dashboard): organization admins and the platform owner can open the page; everyone else is redirected to the home screen. If you are an org admin the page loads but says \"Owner access required to view this dashboard.\" \u2014 the data behind it is platform-owner only.\n- Lab (/lab): any signed-in user can open the page, but it shows \"Restricted to platform owners.\" unless you are the platform owner. No lab data is ever sent to other roles.\n- Integrations (/connections) and everything under Marketplace: organization admins and the platform owner only. Other roles are quietly redirected to the home screen instead of seeing the page.\n- Everything else \u2014 scanning, results, ports, cables, topology, firmware, specifications, profile and history \u2014 is open to every signed-in member.\n\nSteps to fix: if you genuinely need one of those screens, ask your organization admin to change your role (they can promote a member to site manager; only the platform owner can create organization admins, and only RackTrack staff hold the owner role). Signing out and back in isn't necessary and won't change anything, though it does refresh your role if it was just changed.\n\n(Note for support: \"Insufficient permissions\" is the raw 403 response from the API \u2014 customers do not see that wording on screen.)",
      "symptoms": [
