    {
      "question": "After signing in I land on the Organizations console instead of the Scan screen (or the other way round). Did I sign in as the wrong person?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 RackTrack routes you by your role automatically, and there is no role picker on the Sign in screen.\n\n- If you're a platform owner or an organization admin, signing in takes you straight to the Organizations console.\n- Everyone else (site managers and members) goes to the Scan screen, or back to whatever page you were trying to open when you were asked to sign in.\n- If your organization hasn't been approved yet (or was rejected or deactivated), you land on the \"Waiting for approval\" screen instead \u2014 whatever your role. Only the platform owner is never held there.\n\nSo landing somewhere unexpected usually means the account you signed in with has a different role than you assumed \u2014 for example, you signed up and created your own organization, which makes you its admin.\n\nSteps to check: open Profile. It shows your username, email and your Site, and \u2014 if you're an owner or an organization admin \u2014 an \"Administration\" section with a link to the Owner Dashboard or Organization Dashboard. If that Administration section is there, you're an admin or the owner; if it isn't, you're a site manager or member. (Profile doesn't print your role as a label.) If the role is wrong, ask your organization admin to change it \u2014 only the platform owner can create or edit organization admins.",
