    {
      "question": "I tapped Sign in and nothing happens \u2014 the button just spins.",
      "answer": "A spinning Sign in button means the request went out and RackTrack is still waiting for the server to answer. The button stays disabled until the answer (or the failure) comes back.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Give it up to about a minute. On a weak datacenter signal the round-trip can be slow.\n2. If it never resolves, close and reopen the app, then try again. (You can't double-submit while it's spinning \u2014 the button is disabled \u2014 but avoid many rapid retries: sign-in attempts are throttled per account, and once you exceed the limit you'll see the error \"rate_limited\" and need to wait a moment before trying again.)\n3. If it hangs again, treat it as \"server unreachable\": check that you have working internet, and ask your administrator whether the RackTrack server is up. There is no client-side timeout on sign-in, so a dead connection will spin indefinitely rather than showing an error.\n\nAlso check the obvious: if you left the username or password box empty, RackTrack does not send anything at all and instead shows \"Enter your username and password.\" straight away. The Organization box is optional and can be left blank.",
