      "question": "The report window says \"Could not open report\" \u2014 what do I do?",
      "answer": "The report opens with a short-lived pass that RackTrack fetches in the background. That message means fetching the pass failed.\n\nDo this, in order:\n1. **Close the window and tap View again.** A fresh pass is requested every time, so a one-off network blip clears itself.\n2. If the message ends in **HTTP 401**, your session was not accepted. In most cases RackTrack detects this itself and returns you to the sign-in screen \u2014 sign back in and reopen the scan. If you are left on the report window, sign out and back in manually.\n3. If the message ends in **HTTP 404**, RackTrack cannot find that rack for your account. Either the scan does not exist (a mistyped or deleted rack ID), or it belongs to a different Site from yours \u2014 for example someone sent you a rack ID from another Site. Check the rack ID, and if it is someone else's rack, ask its owner to share the report with you instead.\n4. If you have no signal or you are off the datacenter network, reconnect and retry \u2014 the report is generated on the server, not on your phone.",
