    {
      "question": "The Share button spins for ages and then fails \u2014 how long should it take?",
      "answer": "A share happens in two steps, each with its own limit.\n\nFirst RackTrack renders the report as a PDF using a headless browser. Loading the report page is allowed up to **60 seconds**, and the PDF render takes a little longer on top of that. If this step fails you get \"Could not generate the report. Please try again.\"\n\nThen the message is sent to Teams, Outlook or Slack. That sending step gets **two minutes**; if it hasn't finished, RackTrack stops it and the share fails. The two minutes are for the send only, so a slow share can exceed two minutes overall.\n\nA scan with several large photos genuinely takes longer to share than a small one, and the very first share after the server has been restarted is the slowest because the headless browser has to start up (about a second).\n\nIf you hit a timeout: wait a moment and tap **Share** again \u2014 the second attempt is usually faster because the browser is now warm. If it times out repeatedly, use **View \u2192 Download PDF** and send the file yourself.",
