    {
      "question": "The photos in my report look lower quality than in the app",
      "answer": "That is intentional. Before the report is built, RackTrack makes a smaller copy of every scan image that is 500 KB or larger: resized to 1400 pixels wide (never enlarged) and saved as JPEG at quality 76. The report embeds those copies.\n\nThe reason: the report is a single self-contained file with the images baked in, so you can save it, email it and open it offline. At full resolution a rack render is several megabytes, and a report that heavy black-screens inside a phone's viewer.\n\nIf you need the full-resolution image, use the photo shown on the scan result screen rather than the one in the report. Images already below 500 KB are embedded untouched, and if the resizing step cannot run for a particular image the original is embedded unchanged.",
