    {
      "question": "Who is allowed to open or share a rack report?",
      "answer": "Access to a report follows access to the rack it belongs to. There is no admin-only report and no separate permission you can be granted for reports on their own.\n\n- **Members and site managers** can open, download and share reports for racks scanned by **their own Site**. A rack belonging to another Site reads as \"not found\".\n- **Organization admins** can reach any rack owned by any Site inside their own organization.\n- **The platform owner** can reach any rack on the platform.\n- Not signed in at all gives \"Authentication required\" rather than not-found.\n\nSo if a colleague sends you a raw rack ID and you get a not-found error, it is almost certainly a rack in a different Site \u2014 your account is fine, the rack just is not yours.\n\nTwo ways your colleague can get it to you: ask them to share the report by Teams, Outlook or Slack (the PDF travels fine across Sites), or have them send you the report link itself. A shared report link carries a short-lived, single-rack access token, so it opens for you even across Sites \u2014 but only for that one rack, and only until the token expires. It does not give you access to anything else in their Site.",
