      "question": "What is the Incident Report I see when working from a ServiceNow ticket?",
      "answer": "When you scan while working a ServiceNow incident (ticket mode), the **View** button opens a purpose-built panel titled **Incident Report** with the incident number underneath, instead of the normal scan report.\n\nIt shows five blocks:\n- **Incident** \u2014 the short description, priority, and when it was opened.\n- **Image** \u2014 the rack or result photo, or \"not available\".\n- **Port Located** \u2014 the device and interface alias (or \"port N\"), plus rack name, model and management IP from the CMDB.\n- **Output** \u2014 a live sample from the switch: link active/idle, LLDP neighbour and its remote port and management IP, MAC count, the lookup method, and the time it was taken. If the sample failed you get \"Live sample failed: <reason>\"; before the first sample it reads \"no live sample yet\".\n- **Suggestions** \u2014 a plain-English recommendation that depends on what the live sample found:\n  - port confirmed active after being down: \"Port is active now \u2014 cable was attached at <time>. Incident likely resolved; verify with monitoring, then close the ticket.\"\n  - port currently up: \"Port is currently active. Issue may be intermittent \u2014 watch for re-flaps over the next few minutes.\"\n  - port down: \"No traffic on this port right now. Verify the cable is plugged in on both ends, check the far-end device power/NIC status, then re-monitor.\"\n  - SSH failed: \"Cannot reach the switch over SSH to verify. Check mgmt connectivity to <mgmt IP>.\"\n  - before any sample: \"Waiting for first live sample.\"\n\nThe panel itself is view-only \u2014 there is no download or export button inside it. To get something shareable, use the **Share** chip on the results page (it works the same in ticket mode) or post a work note back to the incident.",
