      "question": "I'm pointing the camera at the rack but the shutter won't take the picture. How do I make it fire?",
      "answer": "The shutter is switched off until three checks all pass: the rack has to fill the frame, the light has to be good enough, and the camera has to be steady. The single line of text under the guide box tells you which one is failing:\n\n- \"Move closer so the rack fills the frame\" \u2014 step towards the rack.\n- \"Move to better lighting\" \u2014 change your position or angle away from the light behind the rack.\n- \"Hold steady \u2014 keep still for focus\" \u2014 brace your elbows and wait a moment.\n- \"Starting camera\u2026\" \u2014 the camera has not finished opening yet, just wait.\n\nOnce it says \"Looks great \u2014 tap the shutter below\", the shutter works.\n\nThis only applies to photos. In Video mode the shutter is available as soon as the camera is ready.",
