    {
      "question": "The app says my photo isn't good enough. What are Retake and Proceed anyway?",
      "answer": "When a photo or video fails a quality check you get a warning with the reason and two buttons.\n\n- Retake clears the file so you can take or choose another. This is almost always the right choice.\n- Proceed anyway runs the analysis on the file regardless, with the quality checks turned off (on your device and on the server). A genuinely poor photo then comes back with devices missing, or with an empty rack.\n\nMessages that give you these two buttons:\n- \"Image resolution is low (W\u00d7H). Results may be inaccurate.\" \u2014 the shorter side of the picture is under 480 pixels.\n- \"The image looks blurry. Results may be inaccurate.\"\n- On a video: \"Video resolution is low\", \"Video is too short\" (must be at least 1 second) or \"Video is too long\" (keep it under 120 seconds).\n\nOne message looks similar but does NOT offer Proceed anyway: \"Please upload a clearer photo of the rack \u2014 keep the camera steady and make sure the full rack fits in the frame.\" That appears as a plain error with no buttons, and means the app could not open the image file at all. Take a fresh photo or pick a different file.\n\nNote: HEIC/HEIF photos (the iPhone default format) skip the on-device checks entirely \u2014 the server validates those after upload.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Retake or Proceed anyway",
        "Image resolution is low",
        "The image looks blurry",
        "Please upload a clearer photo of the rack",
        "rack came back empty"
      ],
