      "answer": "RackTrack asks you to check its work with plain yes/no questions as you work through a result. Answering No lets you set the correct value, and your correction is saved to the scan.\n\nThe questions you may see, once you have a device selected:\n- \"Detected as <type> \u2014 right?\" \u2014 the device type. Answer No and pick the real one.\n- \"Detected N RJ45 ports \u2014 right?\" (or \"Detected N total ports (\u2026) \u2014 right?\" when other port types were found) \u2014 appears once you have answered the device-type question. Answer No and pick 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48, or type your own number. This question is not asked for PDUs, which have power outlets rather than RJ45 ports \u2014 the Power card covers those.\n- \"Port N on <device> \u2014 right?\" \u2014 after you have located a port. Answer No and pick the real port number.\n- \"Cable colour is <colour> \u2014 right?\" \u2014 only when the port is shown as connected and a cable colour was detected. Answer No and pick the real colour.\n\nEach question shows Yes and No buttons. Choosing No replaces them with \"What is it actually?\" and a dropdown of choices; if your answer is not in the list, choose \"Other (type it)\" and a box appears for you to type it. Press Submit to save \u2014 you will see \"Saving\u2026\" and then \"Thanks for the feedback.\", after which the question disappears. If you come back to something you have already corrected, it shows a short confirmation line instead of asking again.",
