      "answer": "Open the rack, then Switches, and pick the switch you want.\n\nIf the card shows the tag \"Not detected\" next to Identification, the app could not read the label from your photo. Tap Enter make / model and type them in \u2014 the lookups need both. (If only one is missing the link says Add model or Add vendor instead; once you have typed something it says Edit.)\n\nThen use the tab strip on the card: Specifications, Firmware, SFP Advisor. Open Firmware. If it says \"No firmware version recorded.\", tap Enter version and type the version you are running.\n\nIf you see \"Latest version unknown\", that does NOT mean you are up to date \u2014 it means RackTrack could not confirm the newest version. Follow the \"Check site \u2197\" link to the vendor's own download page and look yourself.\n\nImportant: anything you type here is saved in this browser only. It does not reach the server, your CMDB, or your colleagues, and it is lost if you clear your browsing data or switch device.",
