      "question": "How do I see the rack as a diagram or in 3D?",
      "answer": "Open the rack's results, then the Topology tab (on a laptop or iPad landscape it's \"Topology\" in the left sidebar).\n\nAt the top there is a 2D / 3D toggle. 2D draws the rack as a flat elevation \u2014 a numbered column of U slots (U01, U02, \u2026) with empty slots marked, like the drawing on the cabinet door. 3D puts the same rack in space; drag to orbit and scroll to zoom.\n\nClick any device and the panel at the bottom fills in with its details (type, U position, model, management IP), the peers it is connected to, and a table of its ports showing how many are connected and how many are free. You can also click a cable or a link to inspect it.\n\nIf you see \"Topology is being prepared\", the drawing is still being built in the background after your scan. Wait a moment and tap Retry. The message itself explains it should appear on its own, and that rescanning regenerates it.",
