      "question": "How do I find out what changed on a port, and when?",
      "answer": "Open the rack and go to Drift (on a phone it is behind the More button in the rack tab strip). There is also a standalone Port history & drift page.\n\n1. The monitored switch appears at the top, tagged Streaming when it is being watched, or Paused when it is not.\n2. Below it is the Interface inventory \u2014 a grid of every port, colour-coded: link up, link down, unknown. Click the port you care about.\n3. The panel that opens has three tabs: Specs, Timeline and History (History shows a count of changes).\n4. On Timeline, use the Window dropdown to widen the view \u2014 the choices are Last 1 Hour, Last 3 Hours, Last 12 Hours, Last 1 Day and Last 1 Week. This is how you tell a one-off outage from a port that has been flapping for a fortnight.\n5. The circular arrows button next to the switch name is Poll now \u2014 it checks the switch immediately instead of waiting for the next scheduled pass. You can press it at most 5 times a minute; beyond that you get \"rate limit: max 5 manual polls per minute\".\n\nIf it says \"Waiting for first poll\u2026\" and never changes, no switch is being monitored \u2014 ask an administrator to set one up. Note the background poller runs on a long interval (hourly by default), so use Poll now if you need fresh data immediately.",
