      "question": "How do I reopen a scan I did earlier?",
      "answer": "Open PROFILE and scroll to Recent Scans.\n\nEvery rack you have scanned is listed newest first, with a thumbnail, its rack ID, how many devices, units and ports it found, and how long ago it was. Tap any row to reopen the full result. (As a regular member you see your own scans; site and org admins see more.)\n\nOnly the five most recent are shown at first. If you have more, a button underneath reads \"Show all N scans\" \u2014 tap it to reveal the rest, and \"Show less\" to collapse them again.\n\nIf you have never scanned anything, you get \"No scans yet.\" with a \"Start your first scan\" button.\n\nRecent Scans is the dependable way back to an older rack. On a laptop, desktop browser or iPad in landscape, the rack links in the left sidebar (Overview, Ports, Topology, Network, Switches, Drift) only ever point at the rack you are currently working on \u2014 they are cleared the moment you open the Scan page to start a new one, and a page refresh clears them too. On a phone there are no rack links in the bottom bar at all. (The old /history address redirects to Profile.)",
