    {
      "question": "How do I register a rack in the CMDB after a scan?",
      "answer": "After a scan, if RackTrack finds equipment your configuration database has no record of, it raises the registration ticket for you and shows you a box asking you to approve it. You only need to approve.\n\n1. Finish a scan and stay on the results screen. Within about half a minute a box headed \"Ticket submitted\" appears, showing a Reference number and the note \"Submitted for approval. Approve below to register the discovered inventory in the configuration database now.\"\n2. Tap Approve. (Close dismisses the box \u2014 your scan is unaffected, but the rack stays unregistered, and it will not reappear for that rack until you scan again in a new session.)\n3. It shows \"Synchronizing\u2026\", then \"Successfully registered\", listing the devices, ports, cables and rack size that were written to your records.\n4. Tap Done.\n\nNotes:\n- The box only appears on a freshly completed scan. Reopening an old rack from your history will not show it.\n- If nothing appears, either the rack is already registered, nothing was missing from your records, or no configuration database is connected for your organization.\n- If approval fails you are returned to the same screen with a message such as \"Request to ServiceNow timed out \u2014 try again\"; tap Approve again.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Rack not registered in CMDB",
        "Raise Ticket",
        "how do I register a rack",
        "Successfully registered",
        "Not now"
      ],
      "rootCause": "CmdbApprovalModal state machine: unregistered -> Raise Ticket -> pending -> Approve -> syncing -> registered.",
