      "question": "How do I use the Operations Console, and how do I clear the log?",
      "answer": "Platform owner only. Open Console in the sidebar, or go to /dashboard. (The old /logs address redirects here.)\n\nThe page is titled Operations Console and has two tabs:\n- Operations \u2014 \"Everything happening across RackTrack \u2014 who's scanning, what's working, what's failing.\"\n- Logs \u2014 \"Live application log \u2014 email delivery, errors, and requests as the server records them.\"\n\nIn the header there are two controls that apply to whichever tab you are on: a Live toggle (auto-refresh on / auto-refresh paused) and a Refresh button for a one-off reload.\n\nTo start the log fresh, open the Logs tab and press Clear log. It asks you to confirm first \u2014 \"Delete all N stored log entries and start fresh? This cannot be undone.\" The button reads Clearing\u2026 while it works. This cannot be undone.",
