      "answer": "Open the scan result, pick the device from the Device list, and look for the question **\"Detected N RJ45 ports \u2014 right?\"** (if the device has more than just RJ45 jacks it reads \"Detected N total ports (\u2026) \u2014 right?\"). Tap **No**, then either choose 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48 from the dropdown, or pick **Other (type it)** and type the real number. Tap Submit.\n\nRackTrack does not just record your number \u2014 it re-runs port detection on that device using your count as the target: if the model had found more ports than you say exist it trims to your count, and if it found fewer it lays out an exact grid of your count (keeping the connected/empty status of the ports it did find) and redraws the port picture with the corrected numbering. The device then shows **\"Port count corrected \u2014 you set this\"**.\n\nTwo things to know:\n\n- This question only appears **after** you have answered the device-type question above it (\"Detected as <type> \u2014 right?\"). RackTrack deliberately asks one thing at a time. If you don't see the port-count question, answer the device-type question first.\n- The question is **not shown for PDUs**. A PDU has power outlets rather than RJ45 ports, so RackTrack skips it there \u2014 the Power card summarises the outlets instead.",
