      "question": "The cable colour is wrong \u2014 it says Blue but the cable is grey.",
      "answer": "On the port view, answer **No** to **\"Cable colour is <colour> \u2014 right?\"** and pick the real colour. Twelve swatches are offered: Black, Blue, Brown, Green, Grey, Orange, Pink, Red, White, Yellow, Violet, Aqua \u2014 plus a free-text box if yours isn't one of them. The colour repaints straight away and the port shows **\"Cable colour: <colour> \u2014 you set this\"**.\n\nWhy it gets it wrong: colour is judged from a small crop of your photo, so lighting, shadow and camera white balance can push one colour towards another. RackTrack also only knows a fixed list of colour/connector combinations it was trained on, so a colour outside that list is forced into the nearest one it does know.\n\nNote that cable colour is only worked out for ports RackTrack believes have a cable in them. If the port isn't shown as connected, there is no colour to correct and the question won't appear.",
