    {
      "question": "What does \"Not fully sure about this cable (42% confidence)\" mean? Should I trust it?",
      "answer": "No \u2014 treat it as a guess and check with your own eyes.\n\nRackTrack shows this warning whenever its confidence in reading the cable drops below 50%. The exact wording is: *\"Not fully sure about this cable (N% confidence) \u2014 the photo resolution may be too low to read it clearly. Please check the cable and its colour, and correct them below if they're wrong.\"*\n\nIt almost always means the photo was too low-resolution, too dark, or too far away for that particular port. What to do:\n\n- Look at the actual cable and use the **\"Cable colour is <colour> \u2014 right?\"** question just below the warning to set the correct value.\n- If several ports on the same device are hedging, the photo itself is the problem \u2014 retake it closer, straight-on, with more light, and rescan.\n\nA confidence figure is shown for a reason: the app is telling you it may be wrong. Above 50% you get no warning, but that is not a guarantee of correctness either.",
