    {
      "question": "I rescanned a rack after changing equipment, but RackTrack showed me the old result.",
      "answer": "Yes \u2014 this is expected behaviour, and there are two separate reasons it can happen.\n\n**1. You uploaded the identical photo.** RackTrack identifies a scan by the content of the image, so re-uploading the exact same file returns the earlier result instantly (with your corrections still applied), rather than re-analysing it. The time in Recent Scans is refreshed so it shows as scanned now.\n\n**2. You confirmed the rack's layout previously.** Once a rack layout has been confirmed, RackTrack fingerprints that rack photo. A later photo of the same rack that looks near-identical serves the confirmed result instead of re-detecting. This is deliberately strict \u2014 a re-shoot from a noticeably different angle falls through to a fresh detection rather than risking showing you another rack's data.\n\nIf you have physically changed the rack, take a **noticeably different photo** \u2014 a different distance or angle, or a shot that shows the new equipment clearly. That produces a new fingerprint and forces a fresh analysis.\n\nThere is currently no button in the app to force a fresh re-analysis of an unchanged photo. If a user is stuck on a stale result and cannot get a different-enough photo, escalate.",
      "symptoms": [
        "rescan shows old result",
        "changed the rack but results are the same",
        "scan returned instantly",
        "stale scan result",
        "servedFromConfirmed"
      ],
      "rootCause": "Two bypasses in POST /api/analyze: (a) content-hash cache \u2014 computeRackId(tmpPath) hits an existing device_unit_map.json and returns cached; (b) confirmed-rack bypass \u2014 find_confirmed_rack matches on pHash (HAMMING_TOL 6) then a strict embedding threshold _RACK_SIM_THRESH = 0.96. The server honours a forceFresh flag, but grep shows no client code sends it, so there is no UI escape hatch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/app.js",
          "lines": "2265-2277",
          "snippet": "// \u2500\u2500 Confirmed-rack bypass \u2500\u2500\n// A re-shot photo of a rack the user already CONFIRMED gets a new content\n// hash, so it misses the cache above. If it perceptually matches a confirmed\n// rack, serve that confirmed result instead of re-detecting ...\n// Strict thresholds guard against a wrong-rack match.\nconst _forceFresh = req.body?.forceFresh === '1' || req.body?.forceFresh === 'true';"
        },
        {
          "file": "pipeline/active_learning/store.py",
          "lines": "231-236",
