      "question": "I get \"Camera access denied. Allow camera permission or use Upload.\"",
      "answer": "RackTrack asked your phone or browser for the camera and was refused, so the camera view is replaced by that message with a crossed-out camera icon. (The same message also appears if the device has no usable camera at all.)\n\nFix it in one of these ways:\n\n\u2022 **On iPhone/iPad**: Settings \u2192 RackTrack \u2192 turn **Camera** on, then reopen the app.\n\u2022 **On Android**: Settings \u2192 Apps \u2192 RackTrack \u2192 Permissions \u2192 **Camera** \u2192 Allow.\n\u2022 **In a desktop browser**: click the padlock/camera icon in the address bar, allow the camera for this site, then reload.\n\nIf you tapped \"Don't allow\", the prompt will not reappear on its own \u2014 you have to change it in settings.\n\n**You do not need the camera at all to scan.** On the Scan screen there are two tabs, **Upload** and **Camera**. Tap **Upload** and you get three mode buttons just below it: **SINGLE** (one photo), **MULTI** (2-8 photos stitched together for a tall rack) and **VIDEO** (a 1-120 second clip, useful for a whole row of racks). Each one opens your photo/file picker. This path produces exactly the same results as the camera and is the normal route on an iPad or a computer.",
