      "question": "I picked a photo and got \"The image looks blurry. Results may be inaccurate.\" \u2014 should I press Proceed anyway?",
      "answer": "RackTrack checked the photo before uploading it and found it isn't sharp enough. You get two buttons:\n\n\u2022 **Retake** \u2014 clears the photo so you can take or pick a better one. **This is almost always the right choice.**\n\u2022 **Proceed anyway** \u2014 sends the blurry photo through regardless.\n\nWhy Retake matters: pressing **Proceed anyway** doesn't just skip this warning, it switches off *every* later safety check too. So a genuinely unusable photo comes back as an empty or badly wrong rack instead of an honest error. If your rack \"came back empty\", this is usually why.\n\nTo get a sharp photo: hold the phone still for a second before shooting, tap the screen to focus, and make sure there's enough light \u2014 phones drop the shutter speed in dim aisles, which is what causes most of this blur.",
