    {
      "question": "\"The image appears tilted. Please hold the phone straight and retake.\"",
      "answer": "RackTrack looks at the rack's vertical rails in your photo. If the whole picture is rotated by more than **6 degrees**, or if the lines on the left side of the frame and the lines on the right side disagree by more than **5 degrees** (which means you were standing off to one side), it stops and asks you to retake.\n\n**How to fix it:**\n1. Stand square in front of the rack, not off to one side.\n2. Hold the phone upright, not rolled left or right \u2014 the rack rails should run straight up and down the screen, parallel to the edges of the frame.\n3. Step back far enough that the rails run the full height of the frame; RackTrack needs to see several full-length vertical lines to judge the angle.\n\nRetake rather than proceeding \u2014 a tilted photo mis-assigns devices to the wrong U positions, which is worse than no result.\n\nNote: shooting up or down at the rack is a different problem. That produces the separate message \"The image appears to be taken from a side angle. Results may not be accurate.\" \u2014 a warning rather than a stop. If you see that one instead, move to about the middle height of the rack and retake.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"The image appears tilted. Please hold the phone straight and retake.\"",
        "Devices assigned to the wrong U numbers"
      ],
      "rootCause": "pipeline/quality_check.py check_tilt: weighted average of near-vertical Hough lines exceeding TILT_TOLERANCE_DEG (6.0), or left/right rail averages diverging by more than PERSPECTIVE_TOLERANCE_DEG (5.0).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "pipeline/quality_check.py",
          "lines": "20-21",
          "snippet": "TILT_TOLERANCE_DEG = 6.0           # was 4.0\nPERSPECTIVE_TOLERANCE_DEG = 5.0    # was 3.0"
        },
        {
          "file": "pipeline/quality_check.py",
          "lines": "123-130",
          "snippet": "if abs(overall) > TILT_TOLERANCE_DEG:\n        return {\n            \"ok\": False,\n            \"kind\": \"angle\",\n            \"retryable\": True,\n            \"error\": \"The image appears tilted. Please hold the phone straight and retake.\","
        },
        {
          "file": "pipeline/quality_check.py",
          "lines": "136-142",
          "snippet": "if skew > PERSPECTIVE_TOLERANCE_DEG:\n            return {\n                \"ok\": False,\n                \"kind\": \"angle\",\n                \"retryable\": True,\n                \"error\": \"The image appears tilted. Please hold the phone straight and retake.\","
        }
