    {
      "question": "\"This rack is heavily covered by cables\" \u2014 it won't scan my patched-up rack.",
      "answer": "RackTrack looked at your photo and worked out that cables, not equipment faces, dominate the view \u2014 either because cable edges outnumber device edges, or because a large share of the picture is brightly-coloured patch cable. It tells you which, e.g. \"cable edges dominate (2.4x device edges)\" or \"41% of view is colored cables\".\n\nThe message asks you to **take additional photos from the left and right sides of the rack so we can see behind the cable bundles, or proceed with this image (results may miss devices)**.\n\nWhat to do, in order:\n1. If you can, **dress or lift the cable bundle** aside briefly and reshoot square-on. This gives by far the best result.\n2. Otherwise shoot from slightly left and slightly right of centre so the gaps between bundles reveal different devices, and use the **MULTI** mode to submit them together.\n3. Only as a last resort press **Proceed anyway** \u2014 the scan will run, but devices hidden behind cable bundles will simply be missing from the unit map.\n\nA milder version of this appears as a warning after the scan: \"Cables cover much of the rack \u2014 some devices behind cable bundles may not be detected. Side-angle photos would improve accuracy.\" That one lets the scan through but tells you to expect gaps.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"This rack is heavily covered by cables \u2014 cable edges dominate (N.Nx device edges)\"",
        "\"NN% of view is colored cables\"",
        "\"Cables cover much of the rack \u2014 some devices behind cable bundles may not be detected.\"",
        "Devices missing from the unit map on a densely patched rack"
      ],
      "rootCause": "pipeline/quality_check.py check_occlusion uses two independent signals on the central region \u2014 vertical/horizontal edge magnitude ratio and vivid-saturation pixel fraction. Hard fail at ratio >= 2.10 or sat_frac >= 0.38; soft warning at ratio >= 1.45 or sat_frac >= 0.22.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "pipeline/quality_check.py",
          "lines": "47-51",
          "snippet": "OCCLUSION_NONHORIZ_RATIO = 1.45    # non_horizontal/horizontal edge mag \u2192 \"warning\"\nOCCLUSION_NONHORIZ_HARD  = 2.10    # above this \u2192 \"hard\" (offer multi-angle)\nOCCLUSION_SAT_FRAC_WARN  = 0.22    # fraction of high-saturation pixels \u2192 warning\nOCCLUSION_SAT_FRAC_HARD  = 0.38    # fraction of high-saturation pixels \u2192 hard"
