    {
      "question": "\"Please take the photo from the front of the rack \u2014 we need to see the devices and ports face-on.\"",
      "answer": "The analysis ran all the way through but found **zero devices** in the finished result, so RackTrack discarded the scan rather than showing you an empty rack.\n\nUsual causes:\n\u2022 You shot the **rear** of the rack (cable spaghetti and power leads, no faceplates).\n\u2022 You were side-on rather than square to the rack, or it was too dark.\n\u2022 The rack door was shut, or glass/mesh was between you and the equipment.\n\u2022 You were too far away for any faceplate to be readable.\n\n**Fix:** open the front door, stand square-on far enough back that the whole rack fits inside the guide box, and reshoot. If the shutter will not fire, the hint line under the guide box names the one quality check still failing.\n\nRelated messages:\n\n\u2022 **\"This doesn't look like a server rack. Point the camera at the front of a rack so its devices and ports are visible.\"** \u2014 same underlying problem, but caught immediately instead of after a long wait, because a quick pre-check found no devices before the full analysis started.\n\n\u2022 **\"Please upload a clearer photo of the rack \u2014 keep the camera steady and make sure the full rack fits in the frame.\"** \u2014 most often means devices were found but fewer than three rack units were mapped, i.e. only a sliver of the rack is in shot, so step back until the whole cabinet is in frame. Note that RackTrack also falls back to this same message if the analysis fails for an unrelated reason, so if reshooting a clearly-framed full-rack photo keeps producing it, it is not your photo \u2014 escalate.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"Please take the photo from the front of the rack \u2014 we need to see the devices and ports face-on.\"",
        "\"Please upload a clearer photo of the rack \u2014 keep the camera steady and make sure the full rack fits in the frame.\"",
        "Long analysis then an error instead of results"
      ],
      "rootCause": "Post-pipeline gates in POST /api/analyze: deviceCount === 0 \u2192 front-of-rack error; unitCount < 3 \u2192 clearer-photo error. Both are skipped when skipQualityCheck is set.",
