      "question": "The MULTI (tall rack) stitch failed or produced a mangled panorama.",
      "answer": "MULTI takes **2 to 8 overlapping photos** of a rack too tall for one frame and joins them into one tall image before analysing. The screen tells you: \"Take 2-8 overlapping photos of the rack. Any order \u2014 we'll arrange them automatically.\" You do not need to add them in order; RackTrack works out the top-to-bottom sequence itself.\n\nThe errors you may see:\n\u2022 **\"Please upload at least 2 images to stitch (top-to-bottom).\"** \u2014 you only added one. The button reads \"Add 1 more photo\" until you do.\n\u2022 **\"Could not stitch and analyze the rack. Make sure each photo shows the rack front and adjacent shots overlap by ~20\u201340%.\"** \u2014 this is the key one. **Adjacent photos must overlap by roughly 20\u201340%** (about a fifth to two-fifths of the frame). If you shot the top half and the bottom half with no common band, there is nothing for RackTrack to match on.\n\u2022 **\"No devices were detected on the stitched rack \u2014 make sure each photo shows the front of the rack and the shots overlap.\"** \u2014 the join worked but no equipment was found; usually the rear of the rack or a closed door.\n\n**How to shoot it:** start at the top, and for each next photo include roughly the bottom third of what you just captured. Keep the same distance and the same left-right position for every shot \u2014 moving sideways between shots is the most common cause of a bad join. If RackTrack cannot confidently match a pair it butts them flush instead, which shows up as a visible step in the middle of the rack.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"Please upload at least 2 images to stitch (top-to-bottom).\"",
        "\"Could not stitch and analyze the rack. Make sure each photo shows the rack front and adjacent shots overlap by ~20\u201340%.\"",
        "\"No devices were detected on the stitched rack\"",
        "Visible step or duplicated row in the middle of a tall rack result"
      ],
      "rootCause": "POST /api/stitch accepts upload.array('images', 8) and requires >= 2. pipeline/rack_stitch.find_overlap accepts an overlap only when the best template-match score exceeds the median by peak_margin 0.045 within max_overlap_ratio 0.60; otherwise the seam is recorded as uncertain and images are butted flush.",
      "evidence": [
