    {
      "question": "I switched apps while a scan was running and came back to the upload screen \u2014 is my scan lost?",
      "answer": "No. The scan keeps running on the server even though your phone lost the connection.\n\nWhen you start a scan RackTrack quietly notes a ticket for it. When you come back to the app it checks that ticket and, if the scan finished, takes you straight to the results \u2014 you don't need to rescan.\n\nTwo things to know:\n\n\u2022 The ticket lasts **15 minutes from the moment the scan started** (not from when you left the app). If more than 15 minutes have passed since you hit SCAN, the ticket expires and you'll land on the upload screen. The scan itself may well have completed \u2014 check **Profile**, which lists your past scans, before rescanning.\n\n\u2022 If you come back while the scan is still running, RackTrack waits about 45 seconds for it. If it hasn't finished by then you'll see the upload screen, but the ticket is still held \u2014 reopen or re-foreground the app and it will try again and drop you on the results.\n\n\u2022 Rescanning the exact same photo costs you nothing anyway \u2014 an identical image is recognised and returns instantly.\n\n**Tip:** the progress bar deliberately stops at 88% and waits. That's normal \u2014 the bar is an estimate, not a real measurement. Don't background the app just because it looks stuck.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Back on the upload screen after switching apps",
        "Scan appeared to vanish mid-analysis",
        "Progress bar sits at 88%"
      ],
      "rootCause": "ScanPage generates a clientJobId and stores it in localStorage before awaiting; server scan-jobs.js records jobId\u2192rackId. PendingScanResumer polls /api/analyze/result/:jobId on resume. Both TTLs are 15 min. The progress ticker caps at 88 until the response arrives.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "client/src/utils/pendingScan.js",
          "lines": "12",
          "snippet": "const TTL_MS = 15 * 60 * 1000;   // matches the server-side job TTL"
        },
        {
          "file": "server/lib/scan-jobs.js",
          "lines": "22",
