      "question": "\"Your organization is awaiting owner approval before you can scan.\"",
      "answer": "Your account is fine \u2014 the organisation it belongs to isn't in an \"active\" state, and RackTrack blocks scanning until it is. Nothing you can change in the app will lift this.\n\nCheck the message on your Waiting-for-approval screen, because there are three different situations behind the same scan error:\n\n- **\"Waiting for approval\"** \u2014 your organisation has been submitted and is sitting in the platform owner's approval queue. It appears there automatically; you don't need to do anything to put it in front of them. The screen re-checks every few seconds and will let you straight in the moment it's approved, so in most cases waiting is the right move. There's no automatic email to the owner, so if it's been sitting unusually long, a direct nudge is reasonable.\n- **\"Request not approved\"** \u2014 the owner declined the request. Waiting will not change this; contact the platform owner if you think it's a mistake.\n- **\"Organization deactivated\"** \u2014 the owner has switched your organisation off. It will come back on its own if they reactivate it.\n\nOnce the organisation is active, scanning works immediately with no further action from you.\n\n(Technical: POST /api/analyze calls auth.isOrgActive(organizationId), which requires organizations.status === 'active', and returns 403 for pending, rejected or deactivated orgs before the pipeline runs \u2014 server/app.js:2193-2197, server/auth.js:542-546.)",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"Your organization is awaiting owner approval before you can scan.\"",
        "Held on the Waiting for approval screen",
        "Scan button works but every scan is refused"
      ],
      "rootCause": "POST /api/analyze calls auth.isOrgActive(organizationId) and returns 403 for any non-active organization before touching the pipeline.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "server/app.js",
          "lines": "2181-2188",
          "snippet": "const _a = softAuthPayload(req);\n    if (_a?.organizationId && !auth.isOrgActive(_a.organizationId)) {\n      safeUnlink(req.file.path);\n      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Your organization is awaiting owner approval before you can scan.' });"
        }
      ],
