      "question": "The live ports screen says \"The switch didn't respond. Check you're on the same network as the switch, then Retry.\"",
      "answer": "RackTrack tried to log into the switch over the network and got no answer at all within the time allowed.\n\nBy far the most common cause is being on the **wrong network** \u2014 guest Wi-Fi, a mobile hotspot, or a different VLAN from the switch's management address. From those networks the switch simply isn't reachable.\n\nCheck, in this order:\n1. **Are you on the right network?** Get off guest Wi-Fi and onto the network that can reach the switch's management address.\n2. **Is the switch's management address still the same?** RackTrack already retries a short list of known addresses automatically, so a DHCP change usually recovers on its own \u2014 but if the switch moved to an address RackTrack has never seen, every attempt times out.\n3. **Is a firewall or ACL blocking SSH (port 22)** between you and the switch's management address? A silently dropped connection looks identical to \"not responding\".\n\nThen tap **Retry**.\n\nA related wording \u2014 \"The switch didn't respond in time. Check you're on the same network as it, then tap Retry.\" \u2014 means the whole attempt was abandoned after about 38 seconds rather than a single address timing out.\n\nNone of this affects your rack photo scan; the unit map, devices and ports read from the photo are unaffected.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"The switch didn't respond. Check you're on the same network as the switch, then Retry.\"",
        "\"The switch didn't respond in time. Check you're on the same network as it, then tap Retry.\"",
        "Probe failed banner on the live ports view",
        "Long spinner then an error"
      ],
      "rootCause": "portsProbe tries each candidate host with a 10 s per-attempt SSH timeout under a 38 s AbortController watchdog; ssh2 ETIMEDOUT/EHOSTUNREACH/ENETUNREACH are mapped by friendlyProbeError. Server-side _runSwitchCommandRaw defaults to a 20 s kill timer and uses timeoutMs as readyTimeout.",
      "evidence": [
