    {
      "question": "\"Lost the SSH session to the switch \u2014 it may limit simultaneous connections. Tap Retry.\"",
      "answer": "The connection to the switch was established and then dropped. Small managed switches typically allow only **one** SSH session at a time, so this normally means something else already has it \u2014 a colleague on the switch, a terminal window someone left open, or RackTrack's own background check.\n\n**What to do:** wait a moment and tap **Retry** once. Usually the slot frees and the second attempt works.\n\n**What not to do:** don't hammer Retry. On these switches every failed attempt can leave another stuck session behind, which makes the problem worse rather than better.\n\nIf retrying keeps failing, you may see the more specific message: *\"The switch accepted the login but refused a CLI session \u2014 its concurrent-session limit is saturated by stuck sessions. Do NOT keep retrying (each attempt adds another session). Clear it out-of-band: log into the switch web UI and disable/enable SSH, or reboot the switch; then a single probe will succeed.\"* Follow exactly that \u2014 clear it from the switch's own web interface, then try once.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"Lost the SSH session to the switch \u2014 it may limit simultaneous connections. Tap Retry.\"",
