      "question": "The Network View shows \"Network View offline\" and no discovery data.",
      "answer": "The Network View is powered by a separate **Netdisco** discovery server, and RackTrack cannot reach it. The badge at the top reads **Network View offline**.\n\nThis is a setup issue, not something you can fix from the phone. The badge comes from a quick reachability probe of the Netdisco server, so \"offline\" means one of exactly two things:\n\n\u2022 The Netdisco server isn't running (or is running but not accepting connections).\n\u2022 RackTrack is pointed at the wrong address for it. By default it looks for Netdisco at `http://localhost:5000`, overridden with the `NETDISCO_URL` setting.\n\nThe probe gives up after about 4 seconds, so a very slow or unreachable host also lands here.\n\nRackTrack deliberately hides the raw technical text (connection-refused messages, Python tracebacks, bare status codes) behind the friendly offline banner, so \"offline\" is all you'll see even though the underlying cause is more specific \u2014 an administrator will need to check the server logs.\n\n**A different symptom: the badge says \"Network View online\" but no devices appear.** That is not a reachability problem. Two likely causes:\n\n\u2022 Netdisco rejected the login RackTrack used (`NETDISCO_USER` / `NETDISCO_PASSWORD`, defaulting to admin/admin). Credentials do not affect the online/offline badge \u2014 only the data. Requests for the device data time out after 15 seconds.\n\u2022 Netdisco is reachable and authenticated but simply hasn't discovered those devices. Netdisco finds devices by SNMP, and its shipped configuration reads with SNMP **v2 community `public`**, read-only. Devices with a different community or SNMP version won't be seen. That is configured in Netdisco, not RackTrack.\n\n**Everything else keeps working.** The Network View is the only screen that needs Netdisco; your rack scans, unit map, ports, topology and live switch screens are unaffected.",
      "symptoms": [
        "\"Network View offline\" badge",
        "Network view empty with no error text",
        "No devices listed for a rack in Network View",
        "Devices missing from Netdisco but page loads"
      ],
      "rootCause": "netdisco_proxy.js fetches NETDISCO_URL (default http://localhost:5000) with a 15 s AbortSignal timeout and an api_key login using NETDISCO_USER/NETDISCO_PASSWORD (default admin/admin); failures raise 'Netdisco unreachable' 502. NetdiscoPage's looksLikeNetdiscoNoise suppresses ECONNREFUSED/traceback/bare-status text and renders the offline state. Netdisco's own device_auth ships as SNMP v2 community 'public', read-only.",
      "evidence": [
