      "question": "On an iPad or a computer there's no way to take a photo \u2014 where is the scan button?",
      "answer": "On a large screen, use the **Upload** tab rather than the camera \u2014 it is already the tab you land on.\n\nThe scan screen has two tabs, **Upload** and **Camera**, and under Upload three modes: **SINGLE** (one photo), **MULTI** (2\u20138 photos of a tall rack) and **VIDEO**. Drag a file onto the drop zone or tap it to browse. SINGLE and MULTI accept JPG, PNG, HEIC and MP4; VIDEO accepts MP4, MOV and WEBM.\n\nThe Camera tab does work in a desktop browser if a webcam is available, but a webcam pointed at a rack rarely passes the sharpness, framing and lighting checks, so the shutter tends to stay disabled. Upload is the intended path on iPad and desktop.\n\nOnce the file is selected, tap **Analyze Rack**. In MULTI mode the button reads **Add N more photo** until you have at least two photos, then becomes **Stitch & Analyze (N)**. Everything after that is identical to a phone scan.",
