    {
      "question": "I updated a switch in ServiceNow but RackTrack still shows the old details.",
      "answer": "RackTrack keeps the CMDB answer for a rack for up to one minute so the screen loads fast. If you change a switch in ServiceNow, wait about a minute, then leave the Switch Information screen and open it again \u2014 the new model, serial or IP appears.\n\nIf it still shows the old details after a couple of minutes, ask your administrator to open Connections, select the ServiceNow source and press \"Refresh data from this source\". A successful refresh (it reports how many incidents were pulled) also drops the stored copy so the next load is fresh; if the refresh reports an error, the old copy stays until the minute is up. The Connections screen is only available to organization administrators and the platform owner.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Switch Information shows the previous model, serial or IP",
        "Edit made in ServiceNow not visible immediately"
      ],
      "rootCause": "_cmdbCache in app.js serves any cached payload younger than 60000 ms; the cache is only cleared explicitly after a successful incident refresh poll.",
